5
00:00:36.875 --> 00:00:38.875
[distorted splashing]

6
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.750
[eerie music building]

7
00:01:04.958 --> 00:01:06.458
-[gurgling]
-[music fades]

8
00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:13.917
[suspenseful piano music playing]

9
00:01:25.958 --> 00:01:27.958
[foghorn blares]

10
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.208
You're my first catch in days. but

11
00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:34.042
you're too little.

12
00:01:37.792 --> 00:01:39.708
Whoa. look what's coming.

13
00:01:40.375 --> 00:01:42.207
That one looks nasty.

14
00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:44.041
Yeah. it does.

15
00:01:44.042 --> 00:01:46.125
I better get home before it hits.

16
00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:48.667
-See you tomorrow.
-So long.

17
00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.458
[thunder crashing]

18
00:01:58.125 --> 00:02:02.625
[woman] <i>Everyone remembers where they were
the day the rain came.</i>

19
00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:04.582
[car beeps]

20
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:08.042
<i>It was a Sunday. not quite winter.</i>

21
00:02:09.208 --> 00:02:11.833
<i>The forecast had called for sun.</i>

22
00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.666
[man 1 on radio] <i>This low-pressure system
offshore has turned</i>

23
00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.582
<i>and is moving in fast.</i>

24
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:21.457
[man 2] <i>Expect periods of
heavy rain showers across the city today.</i>

25
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.707
<i>with winds gusting up to 30 miles per hour</i>

26
00:02:23.708 --> 00:02:27.166
{\an8}<i>and the threat
of minor coastal flooding and high surf.</i>

27
00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:29.457
{\an8}[man 3] <i>The holidays are a month away.</i>

28
00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:32.749
<i>and hopefully.
the surprise turn in the weather will...</i>

29
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.624
[woman] <i>People went
about their mornings as usual.</i>

30
00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:37.499
{\an8}-Ready?
-Yeah. let's do it.

31
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.542
{\an8}[woman] <i>We lived
close to each other then...</i>

32
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:41.666
{\an8}Okay. bye.

33
00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:44.625
{\an8}[woman] <i>...but it was easy to feel alone.</i>

34
00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.124
{\an8}Guys. come on. It's gonna rain.

35
00:02:49.125 --> 00:02:50.582
{\an8}Yeah. let's go inside.

36
00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:51.666
[thunder crashing]

37
00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.167
[woman] <i>The day the rain came.</i>

38
00:02:54.083 --> 00:02:55.167
<i>we learned</i>

39
00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.250
<i>we were not alone.</i>

40
00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:05.541
[man on radio] <i>Last December
was the warmest on record</i>

41
00:03:05.542 --> 00:03:08.375
<i>for western Washington.
so keep tuned in for updates.</i>

42
00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.292
{\an8}[clattering]

43
00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:21.000
Come on. Come on.

44
00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.542
[woman] <i>And we learned
just how far some will go</i>

45
00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:42.417
<i>to protect their home.</i>

46
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.500
[sloshing]

47
00:03:53.042 --> 00:03:55.000
[beeping]

48
00:04:00.708 --> 00:04:02.332
[dog whining]

49
00:04:02.333 --> 00:04:05.874
Hey. where is everybody?

50
00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:07.375
Where is everybody?

51
00:04:08.083 --> 00:04:10.458
There's my old boy.

52
00:04:21.375 --> 00:04:22.458
Good morning.

53
00:04:24.042 --> 00:04:25.166
[woman sighs]

54
00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:28.791
-I can't believe the kids let me sleep in.
-Was wondering why it was so quiet.

55
00:04:28.792 --> 00:04:30.291
You caught us breakfast?

56
00:04:30.292 --> 00:04:32.792
Oh yeah. Big catch this morning.

57
00:04:34.542 --> 00:04:36.124
World's best fisherman.

58
00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:37.625
-I know.
-Thank you.

59
00:04:39.042 --> 00:04:40.333
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

60
00:04:40.917 --> 00:04:41.999
-Wake up!
-Donuts!

61
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.166
-Whoa!
-[girl] Donuts!

62
00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.124
-[boy] Gimme.
-[girl] Can we make bacon?

63
00:04:45.125 --> 00:04:47.457
-[man] Just calm down. Just... Come on.
-[boy] Bacon!

64
00:04:47.458 --> 00:04:49.666
-[woman] Please leave some for us!
-[man] Vultures.

65
00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.332
-Total vultures.
-[girl] Turn it on!

66
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:52.499
-Okay.
-[girl] Make it work.

67
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.749
[woman] I just gave Cassidy his meds.
and don't feed him any bacon.

68
00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.416
You deserve it more than they do.

69
00:04:57.417 --> 00:04:59.082
[energetic game music playing]

70
00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:00.083
[device bleeps]

71
00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.374
-Dad. the streaming stopped working.
-[rain pattering]

72
00:05:03.375 --> 00:05:06.749
I don't know. I think
this house is really falling apart.

73
00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.374
-I'm ready to move when you are.
-Sure.

74
00:05:08.375 --> 00:05:10.582
A few more lottery tickets
and we should be good to go.

75
00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:11.583
Hey.

76
00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.500
You know I'm just kidding. right?

77
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.042
This isn't all on you.

78
00:05:20.625 --> 00:05:24.625
Oh. the guy is coming tomorrow
to check the cracks in the chimney.

79
00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:26.125
Mm.

80
00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.916
-[scoffs] This is new.
-What?

81
00:05:28.917 --> 00:05:30.791
He thinks our foundation is sinking.

82
00:05:30.792 --> 00:05:33.457
so the only thing
holding the house together is the chimney.

83
00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:36.625
The house collapsing on us
while we're sleeping would be a bummer.

84
00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:39.374
Do you still wanna go buy
a Christmas tree?

85
00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:41.082
-It's raining out there.
-Come on.

86
00:05:41.083 --> 00:05:43.166
Wait. wait. Dad. come on.
You promised. Please.

87
00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:45.499
-[softly] I didn't promise. You promised.
-[kids] Dad!

88
00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.916
-You promised.
-[boy] Dad!

89
00:05:46.917 --> 00:05:48.499
-Who promised you guys?
-[both] You!

90
00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.582
[chuckles]

91
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:51.582
-Yeah. let's go.
-Come on.

92
00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:52.666
Let's buy a tree.

93
00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.227
-[boy] Let's go!
-[girl] I wanna pick!

94
00:05:56.042 --> 00:05:59.124
-Help me put my shoes on.
-You know how to put your shoes on.

95
00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.791
Hey. no scooter in the house.

96
00:06:00.792 --> 00:06:02.582
Come on. Mom! Let's go!

97
00:06:02.583 --> 00:06:06.124
-She always takes forever.
-Then you shouldn't act surprised. right?

98
00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:08.875
Help your sister put her shoes on.
Go wait in the car.

99
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.750
Ann! Let's go!

100
00:06:11.417 --> 00:06:13.332
-Don't rush me.
-I'm not.

101
00:06:13.333 --> 00:06:15.499
I'm hiding from our children.

102
00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.082
Seriously. when can we stop doing
this tree thing?

103
00:06:18.083 --> 00:06:19.999
It's Christmas. you Grinch.

104
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.832
[groaning]

105
00:06:21.833 --> 00:06:23.207
Okay. what did you do?

106
00:06:23.208 --> 00:06:24.707
You have to unlock it. stupid.

107
00:06:24.708 --> 00:06:26.416
-I did. stupid!
-Shut up!

108
00:06:26.417 --> 00:06:28.666
[man] Stop arguing! You're both stupid.

109
00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:30.332
[girl] It won't open because of Graham.

110
00:06:30.333 --> 00:06:33.374
-[Graham] Don't blame me. That was you.
-[girl] You obviously did something!

111
00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:35.791
No. I didn't.
Why do you blame me all the time?

112
00:06:35.792 --> 00:06:38.124
[tense music playing]

113
00:06:38.125 --> 00:06:39.457
[girl] It's <i>all</i> your fault!

114
00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:41.916
This is why <i>I'm</i> the favorite.
and you always cause problems.

115
00:06:41.917 --> 00:06:44.874
-[Graham] Shut up. You're such a baby.
-[girl] I'm not a baby!

116
00:06:44.875 --> 00:06:46.583
I'm 8 years old!

117
00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:48.958
[tense music building]

118
00:06:50.375 --> 00:06:51.832
What did you two do?

119
00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:53.417
-[both] Nothing!
-[girl] Ugh!

120
00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:59.207
[Cassidy whines. barks]

121
00:06:59.208 --> 00:07:01.791
-[man] Quiet. Cass.
-[Cassidy continues barking]

122
00:07:01.792 --> 00:07:03.832
[Ann] Okay. Cass. shush.

123
00:07:03.833 --> 00:07:05.707
Guys. Why aren't you in the car?

124
00:07:05.708 --> 00:07:07.291
-Door won't open.
-Can't get out.

125
00:07:07.292 --> 00:07:09.957
We've tried every door. Nothing will open.

126
00:07:09.958 --> 00:07:12.500
-You guys. Guys.
-I'll try the windows in my room.

127
00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.666
[Cassidy whining]

128
00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:27.833
What? [chuckles] Okay.

129
00:07:32.542 --> 00:07:34.542
[music becomes stirring]

130
00:07:37.292 --> 00:07:39.167
[Cassidy barking]

131
00:07:40.958 --> 00:07:41.958
[scoffs]

132
00:07:44.333 --> 00:07:45.708
[Ann] This is absurd.

133
00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.167
[lights plinking. buzzing]

134
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.457
Yeah. It's a prank. Teenagers.

135
00:07:56.458 --> 00:08:00.166
They glued all the windows and doors shut
or something. right?

136
00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:02.374
No prank. Quiet. Cass!

137
00:08:02.375 --> 00:08:04.083
[Ann] But I don't have any service.

138
00:08:05.542 --> 00:08:07.041
Not connected. No Wi-Fi.

139
00:08:07.042 --> 00:08:10.042
[Ann] Unplug the router
and plug it back in. D'you try that?

140
00:08:10.792 --> 00:08:13.124
-Did you pay the bill?
-[man] Yes.

141
00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.374
[Ann] Cass. quiet!

142
00:08:14.375 --> 00:08:15.791
Do you have signal now?

143
00:08:15.792 --> 00:08:17.582
-No. nothing.
-[girl] Mom. Dad.

144
00:08:17.583 --> 00:08:19.624
I tried the windows in my room.
Nothing's working.

145
00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:22.041
-It's like it's glued shut.
-Every window in there is stuck.

146
00:08:22.042 --> 00:08:25.374
-[Ann] Cass!
-[Cassidy continues barking]

147
00:08:25.375 --> 00:08:27.458
[tense string music building]

148
00:08:32.292 --> 00:08:33.374
-[girl] Dad!
-[Graham] Dad.

149
00:08:33.375 --> 00:08:34.499
Are you okay?

150
00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.124
-[Graham & Ann] Are you okay?
-Yeah.

151
00:08:36.125 --> 00:08:37.582
Yeah. I'm fine.

152
00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.374
[music fades]

153
00:08:39.375 --> 00:08:41.374
-I'm fine.
-[Ann] Okay.

154
00:08:41.375 --> 00:08:42.750
[girl] What is going... Dad!

155
00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:47.291
-I don't understand.
-Okay. stand back.

156
00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:49.666
-Why? Wait. What are you talking about?
-[girl] Dad!

157
00:08:49.667 --> 00:08:51.666
-No. no!
-Stand back. I'll take care of this.

158
00:08:51.667 --> 00:08:52.874
[Ann] Jason. no!

159
00:08:52.875 --> 00:08:54.875
[Cassidy continues barking]

160
00:08:56.125 --> 00:08:57.625
-Just stop!
-Mom!

161
00:08:59.625 --> 00:09:01.624
-[Ann] Stop!
-[girl] Dad!

162
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.625
[tense string music building]

163
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.124
[dramatic drums pounding]

164
00:09:08.125 --> 00:09:09.125
Mom.

165
00:09:16.292 --> 00:09:17.292
Dad.

166
00:09:17.792 --> 00:09:19.792
[Jason grunting]

167
00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.500
Kids.

168
00:09:34.625 --> 00:09:36.042
Dad. look!

169
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.332
-[music fades out]
-[Cassidy stops barking]

170
00:09:41.333 --> 00:09:43.416
-Oh my God.
-[Jason] It's not just us.

171
00:09:43.417 --> 00:09:45.916
-Hey. we can't get out.
-Look. someone's coming.

172
00:09:45.917 --> 00:09:46.958
[Ann] Yeah.

173
00:09:47.458 --> 00:09:49.707
[Jason] That's what's-her-name
from across the street.

174
00:09:49.708 --> 00:09:51.416
-Greg's wife.
-Whatever her name is.

175
00:09:51.417 --> 00:09:53.166
-[Ann] Susan.
-[Jason] Susan!

176
00:09:53.167 --> 00:09:55.082
Susan. go get help!

177
00:09:55.083 --> 00:09:57.333
We're stuck in here! Go get help!

178
00:09:58.125 --> 00:10:00.583
-[Ann] He can't get out either.
-I'll be right back.

179
00:10:01.125 --> 00:10:02.957
Okay. okay. good. She's gonna go get help.

180
00:10:02.958 --> 00:10:04.708
-She's gonna go get help.
-[Jason] Yeah.

181
00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.082
Great. It's okay.

182
00:10:07.083 --> 00:10:09.707
-So we're fine.
-[Jason] Okay. Yeah. I know.

183
00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:11.832
It's... I...

184
00:10:11.833 --> 00:10:12.833
It's okay.

185
00:10:13.625 --> 00:10:15.207
[Jason] Yeah. it's okay. Yeah.

186
00:10:15.208 --> 00:10:17.750
-[foreboding orchestral music playing]
-[metallic banging]

187
00:10:19.792 --> 00:10:21.167
[Jason grunts]

188
00:10:23.792 --> 00:10:24.917
[panting]

189
00:10:29.125 --> 00:10:31.417
[birds tweeting]

190
00:10:40.375 --> 00:10:42.500
[music fades out]

191
00:10:43.083 --> 00:10:46.333
Okay. guys. let's see
what the neighbors are up to.

192
00:10:47.458 --> 00:10:49.624
-You know all the neighbors?
-Pretty much.

193
00:10:49.625 --> 00:10:52.332
Yeah. so the Richardsons are
across the street.

194
00:10:52.333 --> 00:10:54.707
They have three grandchildren.
and I think Max is a dentist.

195
00:10:54.708 --> 00:10:56.749
[Jason] Yeah. That's what's-his-name.

196
00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.166
-Bike boy.
-[Graham] Hmm?

197
00:10:58.167 --> 00:10:59.541
-Bike boy?
-Bike boy?

198
00:10:59.542 --> 00:11:01.791
One of those guys
who wears all that dumb gear.

199
00:11:01.792 --> 00:11:04.249
It's Greg. His wife was the one
who ran to go get help.

200
00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:05.666
Why isn't she back yet?

201
00:11:05.667 --> 00:11:08.582
[Ann] Don't worry. I'm sure
she'll be back with the police soon.

202
00:11:08.583 --> 00:11:10.375
Then there's that nosy guy down there.

203
00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.332
Oof.

204
00:11:12.333 --> 00:11:13.832
-What's his name?
-Oh my God.

205
00:11:13.833 --> 00:11:16.791
Do you know anyone's name here
on this street?

206
00:11:16.792 --> 00:11:18.583
Yeah. this annoying lady with the dog.

207
00:11:19.792 --> 00:11:21.166
Who else?

208
00:11:21.167 --> 00:11:23.833
Oh. yeah. Let's not forget
doofus with the boat.

209
00:11:24.333 --> 00:11:25.582
What was it called?

210
00:11:25.583 --> 00:11:27.041
"Seas the Day"?

211
00:11:27.042 --> 00:11:28.832
Such a doofus.

212
00:11:28.833 --> 00:11:30.499
[girl giggling]

213
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.833
-Good job.
-Mm-hmm.

214
00:11:34.875 --> 00:11:36.292
-Ann.
-Mm?

215
00:11:39.417 --> 00:11:41.416
"This was a one-night stand. LOL."

216
00:11:41.417 --> 00:11:43.291
Oh no!

217
00:11:43.292 --> 00:11:44.666
What's a one-night stand?

218
00:11:44.667 --> 00:11:46.457
-Um...
-It's an adult sleepover.

219
00:11:46.458 --> 00:11:48.707
What's the difference
between an adult sleepover

220
00:11:48.708 --> 00:11:50.375
and a regular sleepover?

221
00:11:51.083 --> 00:11:54.749
Uh... Well. in an adult sleepover...

222
00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:57.457
-You can have as much candy as you want.
-[girl] That sounds fun.

223
00:11:57.458 --> 00:11:59.750
[Jason] I guess so. I don't know.

224
00:12:01.208 --> 00:12:02.916
[curious music playing]

225
00:12:02.917 --> 00:12:04.167
"Government?"

226
00:12:05.083 --> 00:12:06.291
[girl] Hey!

227
00:12:06.292 --> 00:12:08.041
That took a long time.

228
00:12:08.042 --> 00:12:09.208
No. it didn't.

229
00:12:11.042 --> 00:12:14.250
"Maybe. But why?"

230
00:12:18.125 --> 00:12:19.999
"For our safety?"

231
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.708
Oh. look. Doofus with the boat has a sign.

232
00:12:23.708 --> 00:12:25.541
Is that how you spell aliens?

233
00:12:25.542 --> 00:12:26.999
No. honey. it's not.

234
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.291
Why would aliens wanna lock us all
in our houses?

235
00:12:29.292 --> 00:12:30.792
[Ann] They wouldn't. honey.

236
00:12:37.208 --> 00:12:38.458
[Jason] "The whole world?"

237
00:12:45.708 --> 00:12:46.832
[Cassidy grumbles]

238
00:12:46.833 --> 00:12:48.625
[rain pattering]

239
00:12:50.083 --> 00:12:52.124
-Okay. everybody. look at me.
-[music fades out]

240
00:12:52.125 --> 00:12:54.957
We are safe. We are in our home.

241
00:12:54.958 --> 00:12:58.750
We have everything we need here.
but most importantly. we have each other.

242
00:12:59.333 --> 00:13:02.333
-Can I have a donut?
-No. Eat your spaghetti.

243
00:13:02.833 --> 00:13:04.125
But I wanna stress eat.

244
00:13:04.792 --> 00:13:06.667
How do you know about stress eating. Ruth?

245
00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.458
[Ann] Graham.

246
00:13:14.583 --> 00:13:17.917
If you can make it in there.
I can make it out here.

247
00:13:18.958 --> 00:13:21.707
Do you think
the running woman has found help?

248
00:13:21.708 --> 00:13:24.249
Someone's gonna come. I promise.

249
00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:26.083
I think it was the rain.

250
00:13:26.583 --> 00:13:28.208
The rain did this.

251
00:13:28.708 --> 00:13:31.667
No. baby. it's just rain.

252
00:13:33.375 --> 00:13:35.707
-We'll be fine. I promise.
-[long ethereal notes droning]

253
00:13:35.708 --> 00:13:38.667
[Ruth] The rain looked different today.

254
00:13:39.833 --> 00:13:42.125
[Ann] I'm trying to keep it together
for the kids.

255
00:13:42.625 --> 00:13:46.082
But what the hell's going on. Jason?
How is this real? Like. honestly. how?

256
00:13:46.083 --> 00:13:48.666
-I don't know.
-Oh my God. My parents.

257
00:13:48.667 --> 00:13:50.666
They must be freaking out right now.

258
00:13:50.667 --> 00:13:53.207
The Richardsons across the street?

259
00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:54.457
They're okay. right?

260
00:13:54.458 --> 00:13:56.624
I'm sure your parents are okay too.

261
00:13:56.625 --> 00:13:57.791
You're right.

262
00:13:57.792 --> 00:13:59.249
[chilling chords droning]

263
00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.875
I need to show you something.

264
00:14:13.167 --> 00:14:14.333
[Ann] Is that a gun?

265
00:14:14.875 --> 00:14:18.416
Jason. you can't buy a gun
and not tell me.

266
00:14:18.417 --> 00:14:20.457
-I was going to tell you.
-What about the kids?

267
00:14:20.458 --> 00:14:21.458
I know.

268
00:14:23.458 --> 00:14:26.624
-Okay. I've been having this nightmare.
-What? What nightmare?

269
00:14:26.625 --> 00:14:29.916
I woke up a couple weeks ago.
and I felt this thing.

270
00:14:29.917 --> 00:14:32.125
I just... I... I felt we weren't safe.

271
00:14:32.875 --> 00:14:34.167
And you feel safe now?

272
00:14:35.625 --> 00:14:37.374
-I'm sorry.
-Okay.

273
00:14:37.375 --> 00:14:38.416
Okay?

274
00:14:38.417 --> 00:14:39.458
Okay.

275
00:14:44.292 --> 00:14:47.125
Show me how to use the stupid thing
before you put it back.

276
00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:51.750
[car alarm beeping]

277
00:14:53.167 --> 00:14:54.833
[key clicking]

278
00:15:24.375 --> 00:15:25.707
Oh. come on.

279
00:15:25.708 --> 00:15:27.917
-[key clicking]
-Come on.

280
00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.625
Good one. idiot.

281
00:15:37.917 --> 00:15:39.917
[low whirring]

282
00:15:45.583 --> 00:15:47.583
[whirring continues]

283
00:16:01.375 --> 00:16:03.375
[squelching]

284
00:16:06.792 --> 00:16:08.250
What the hell is this?

285
00:16:20.875 --> 00:16:22.167
[Ann] Hey.

286
00:16:26.458 --> 00:16:27.833
I can't break through.

287
00:16:29.292 --> 00:16:33.667
The rain is creating some kind of barrier
around the house.

288
00:16:34.542 --> 00:16:36.666
The same thing going down.

289
00:16:36.667 --> 00:16:38.249
[Ann] Who's doing this?

290
00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:41.707
I don't know. but they've sealed us in.

291
00:16:41.708 --> 00:16:44.416
Are we gonna have to worry
about running out of air?

292
00:16:44.417 --> 00:16:45.958
I checked that too.

293
00:16:48.417 --> 00:16:49.582
Air is getting in.

294
00:16:49.583 --> 00:16:52.249
Okay. Then we wait for the rain to stop.

295
00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:53.417
Come to bed.

296
00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:55.333
Ann.

297
00:16:56.417 --> 00:16:59.250
Whatever is keeping us in here is not...

298
00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.708
man-made.

299
00:17:08.917 --> 00:17:10.917
[Ann] Please hide this from the kids.

300
00:17:23.667 --> 00:17:25.792
[creaking]

301
00:17:28.875 --> 00:17:30.708
[creaking]

302
00:17:39.417 --> 00:17:40.749
[music fades out]

303
00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:42.708
[rain pattering]

304
00:17:48.042 --> 00:17:50.042
[distant bird cawing]

305
00:17:51.042 --> 00:17:53.082
[birds tweeting]

306
00:17:53.083 --> 00:17:54.083
[Jason] Mm.

307
00:18:01.708 --> 00:18:04.167
[gentle music playing]

308
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.208
I already tried it.

309
00:18:21.375 --> 00:18:23.375
[music fades out]

310
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.832
You two seem pretty calm about this.

311
00:18:26.833 --> 00:18:29.916
There's nothing
we could really do about it. right?

312
00:18:29.917 --> 00:18:32.917
Yeah. You guys are the parents.
You'll figure this out.

313
00:18:33.917 --> 00:18:36.083
[curious string music playing]

314
00:18:37.875 --> 00:18:40.167
[Jason] Great. Move that a little. Yeah.

315
00:18:41.542 --> 00:18:45.749
All right. It's time for you guys
to start learning about good music.

316
00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:48.957
You're telling me <i>this</i> is good music?

317
00:18:48.958 --> 00:18:50.917
Yeah. The classics.

318
00:18:52.042 --> 00:18:54.417
Oh. we have a DVD.

319
00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:58.750
Huh.

320
00:18:59.417 --> 00:19:01.999
I guess we have two movies only.

321
00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:06.582
Okay. so now your mom
is gonna talk to you guys about chores.

322
00:19:06.583 --> 00:19:09.166
Okay. look. this isn't a vacation.
You're gonna keep a schedule.

323
00:19:09.167 --> 00:19:10.416
You're gonna make your beds.

324
00:19:10.417 --> 00:19:13.125
You're gonna get dressed every day.
You're gonna brush your teeth.

325
00:19:14.583 --> 00:19:16.207
[Ruth] Cass!

326
00:19:16.208 --> 00:19:18.792
[Jason] <i>We need to focus
on the essentials.</i>

327
00:19:19.958 --> 00:19:21.374
<i>If we ration carefully.</i>

328
00:19:21.375 --> 00:19:24.249
<i>there's no reason
our food can't last us two months.</i>

329
00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:26.499
-Is that food?
-Yes.

330
00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:28.124
I think these are really old.

331
00:19:28.125 --> 00:19:29.875
[Jason] <i>Maybe even longer.</i>

332
00:19:30.375 --> 00:19:31.749
Yeah. we'll eat those last.

333
00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:34.624
<i>As of right now. we still have power.
we have water.</i>

334
00:19:34.625 --> 00:19:37.666
<i>we have gas. but there's no telling
how long any of that's gonna last.</i>

335
00:19:37.667 --> 00:19:41.207
<i>So we have to start treating water
and power as luxuries</i>

336
00:19:41.208 --> 00:19:42.875
<i>that we could lose at any moment.</i>

337
00:19:44.625 --> 00:19:47.874
Hey. this is all temporary.
and we're gonna get through this.

338
00:19:47.875 --> 00:19:50.707
Your mom and I will keep you safe.
I promise.

339
00:19:50.708 --> 00:19:52.624
Team Delgado on three.

340
00:19:52.625 --> 00:19:54.499
-I don't think we need to do this.
-Just do it.

341
00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.832
[Ann] One. two. three.

342
00:19:56.833 --> 00:19:58.291
[all] Team Delgado!

343
00:19:58.292 --> 00:20:00.291
-Can I have a donut now?
-No.

344
00:20:00.292 --> 00:20:02.292
[Cassidy whining]

345
00:20:03.417 --> 00:20:04.542
Oh.

346
00:20:05.167 --> 00:20:06.333
Cass.

347
00:20:09.292 --> 00:20:10.875
Old man.

348
00:20:13.417 --> 00:20:16.417
I can't open this door. okay?
I'm so sorry.

349
00:20:18.292 --> 00:20:20.457
Just pick anywhere you like.

350
00:20:20.458 --> 00:20:22.208
I'll clean it up for you.

351
00:20:29.833 --> 00:20:30.875
Ru.

352
00:20:32.833 --> 00:20:33.917
What did I say?

353
00:20:34.917 --> 00:20:37.874
We act like we're at school
during school time.

354
00:20:37.875 --> 00:20:39.499
Dad. I've already done this chapter.

355
00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.166
-Do it again.
-What's the point of it?

356
00:20:41.167 --> 00:20:44.333
Might sound like a waste of time now.
Graham. but you...

357
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.875
But you're right.
It's a total waste of time.

358
00:20:48.583 --> 00:20:49.708
[Jason sighs]

359
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:51.500
[groans softly]

360
00:20:53.208 --> 00:20:56.708
Okay. You guys wanna learn something real?

361
00:20:57.458 --> 00:20:59.624
-Something you might actually use one day?
-Yeah.

362
00:20:59.625 --> 00:21:00.749
Let's go.

363
00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:03.583
Are you ready?

364
00:21:04.083 --> 00:21:07.541
Are you ready?

365
00:21:07.542 --> 00:21:10.832
Today. you guys are gonna learn
how to gut a fish.

366
00:21:10.833 --> 00:21:13.749
Obviously. we don't have any fish.

367
00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:16.582
but Ruth here. she was kind enough

368
00:21:16.583 --> 00:21:19.832
to donate three of her stuffies
for this lesson.

369
00:21:19.833 --> 00:21:21.166
-Please.
-You're welcome.

370
00:21:21.167 --> 00:21:25.124
Thank you very much.
Now. what are the rules with knives?

371
00:21:25.125 --> 00:21:26.541
Don't cut your fingers off.

372
00:21:26.542 --> 00:21:28.166
-Don't stab your brother.
-What?

373
00:21:28.167 --> 00:21:29.374
Don't stab anyone.

374
00:21:29.375 --> 00:21:31.374
All right. so first thing you're gonna do.

375
00:21:31.375 --> 00:21:33.707
you're gonna cut off
the head and the tail.

376
00:21:33.708 --> 00:21:35.916
You're not gonna eat those parts.

377
00:21:35.917 --> 00:21:40.791
With the head off. you're gonna find
a very convenient hole right here.

378
00:21:40.792 --> 00:21:42.541
at the base of the throat.

379
00:21:42.542 --> 00:21:44.749
And that's where
we're gonna start our incision.

380
00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:47.541
and this will also ensure
that we don't rupture any organ

381
00:21:47.542 --> 00:21:49.582
that can contaminate our meat.

382
00:21:49.583 --> 00:21:54.499
Slice down the middle like this.
and then you start scooping out the guts.

383
00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:58.041
If this was a real fish.
we would wash it out in water.

384
00:21:58.042 --> 00:22:02.707
We could use a faucet. or even better.
we would wash it in the ocean.

385
00:22:02.708 --> 00:22:04.582
How do you know so much about fish?

386
00:22:04.583 --> 00:22:06.208
Because I love the sea.

387
00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:09.291
and I had my own fishing boat.

388
00:22:09.292 --> 00:22:10.249
-Really?
-Mm-hmm.

389
00:22:10.250 --> 00:22:11.374
-Where is it?
-I sold it.

390
00:22:11.375 --> 00:22:13.249
-Why?
-Because kids are expensive.

391
00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:14.750
[Graham] Mm?

392
00:22:15.625 --> 00:22:17.041
Dad. [chuckles]

393
00:22:17.042 --> 00:22:17.999
[Jason chuckles]

394
00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:21.166
Now. open up your fish. and that's
where we're gonna find your fillets.

395
00:22:21.167 --> 00:22:23.041
and that's the part we're gonna eat.

396
00:22:23.042 --> 00:22:25.000
What are you guys doing?

397
00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:26.666
Gutting fish.

398
00:22:26.667 --> 00:22:28.416
Mine's a mermaid.

399
00:22:28.417 --> 00:22:29.541
I see that.

400
00:22:29.542 --> 00:22:32.832
So we're at the "let the kids play
with knives" phase of this.

401
00:22:32.833 --> 00:22:35.249
-Uh... they're learning.
-[Ruth] Yeah.

402
00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:36.749
And we're being careful. Mom.

403
00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:39.041
-And we're having fun.
-Having fun.

404
00:22:39.042 --> 00:22:40.124
Mm.

405
00:22:40.125 --> 00:22:41.250
Mm-hmm.

406
00:22:44.583 --> 00:22:46.625
I wanna know how far this has spread.

407
00:22:48.292 --> 00:22:49.833
Can you ask neighbor farther down?

408
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:52.458
Exactly. like a game of telephone.

409
00:22:57.542 --> 00:23:01.749
So. what time do you
usually start drinking around here?

410
00:23:01.750 --> 00:23:04.416
-Uh. 11:00?
-Uh-huh.

411
00:23:04.417 --> 00:23:05.958
More like 10:30.

412
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.707
Oh no. It's been doing that.

413
00:23:08.708 --> 00:23:10.416
That's exciting.

414
00:23:10.417 --> 00:23:11.500
[Ann] No.

415
00:23:12.375 --> 00:23:15.458
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa!
No. don't throw that away.

416
00:23:15.958 --> 00:23:17.749
-What you doing?
-I'm saving this.

417
00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:19.416
-Oh.
-Yeah.

418
00:23:19.417 --> 00:23:23.208
This goes over here like this.

419
00:23:23.917 --> 00:23:25.166
Lay it in here.

420
00:23:25.167 --> 00:23:27.917
And once it dries.
then we have tomato seeds.

421
00:23:28.417 --> 00:23:29.791
-What?
-I love you.

422
00:23:29.792 --> 00:23:31.499
I know. 'cause I'm amazing.

423
00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:32.667
Yes. you are.

424
00:23:34.042 --> 00:23:36.042
[hopeful string music playing]

425
00:23:47.083 --> 00:23:50.042
[Jason] Five blocks. Everyone the same.

426
00:23:50.875 --> 00:23:51.875
Thanks. Max.

427
00:23:53.250 --> 00:23:54.457
"How are you?"

428
00:23:54.458 --> 00:23:57.833
So far. so good. You?

429
00:24:01.583 --> 00:24:02.583
"Getting by."

430
00:24:03.917 --> 00:24:06.292
"What do you do for a living. Jason?"

431
00:24:07.167 --> 00:24:08.708
I'm an engineer. Max.

432
00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:11.167
Currently unemployed.

433
00:24:13.583 --> 00:24:16.875
[chuckles] Yeah.
My kids have some cavities.

434
00:24:18.250 --> 00:24:20.042
{\an8}Can you come over and fix 'em?

435
00:24:25.583 --> 00:24:27.208
Do you have any food?

436
00:24:27.708 --> 00:24:30.624
Enough for now.

437
00:24:30.625 --> 00:24:31.625
You?

438
00:24:36.958 --> 00:24:38.250
[sighs]

439
00:24:45.500 --> 00:24:46.667
Okay.

440
00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:55.958
[music fades]

441
00:24:59.083 --> 00:25:00.625
[sloshing]

442
00:25:05.125 --> 00:25:07.042
[ominous flute music playing]

443
00:25:21.667 --> 00:25:23.000
[chuckles]

444
00:25:29.458 --> 00:25:31.792
We don't draw on the windows. Ruth.

445
00:25:33.792 --> 00:25:35.375
[Jason] Hey. hey. hey. hey. hey!

446
00:25:38.083 --> 00:25:40.083
[drumbeat playing]

447
00:25:40.750 --> 00:25:42.207
-You.
-[Ann] Uh-oh.

448
00:25:42.208 --> 00:25:43.582
Mom? Can you go?

449
00:25:43.583 --> 00:25:45.166
No. it's all you. girl.

450
00:25:45.167 --> 00:25:46.499
[Ann] Do I have to?

451
00:25:46.500 --> 00:25:48.124
-You have to.
-[Ann] Yes. you have to.

452
00:25:48.125 --> 00:25:50.707
-You have to. you have to. Come on.
-[funky bass line kicks in]

453
00:25:50.708 --> 00:25:51.708
Come on.

454
00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:53.417
Here. Put your foot here.

455
00:25:57.833 --> 00:26:01.416
-["Close To Me" by The Cure playing]
<i>-♪ I've waited hours for this ♪</i>

456
00:26:01.417 --> 00:26:04.041
<i>♪ I've made myself so sick ♪</i>

457
00:26:04.042 --> 00:26:06.082
<i>-♪ I wish I'd stayed... ♪</i>
-[Jason] Come on.

458
00:26:06.083 --> 00:26:09.000
<i>♪ Asleep today ♪</i>

459
00:26:09.583 --> 00:26:12.207
<i>♪ I never thought this day would end ♪</i>

460
00:26:12.208 --> 00:26:16.624
<i>♪ I never thought tonight could ever be ♪</i>

461
00:26:16.625 --> 00:26:19.458
<i>♪ This close to me-hee ♪</i>

462
00:26:21.125 --> 00:26:22.500
<i>♪ Ba-ba-ba-ba. ba-dum ♪</i>

463
00:26:23.583 --> 00:26:25.500
<i>♪ Ba-ba-ba-ba. ba-dum... ♪</i>

464
00:26:26.917 --> 00:26:29.458
No scooters in the house. Come on. I...

465
00:26:30.042 --> 00:26:32.666
<i>♪ Just try to see in the dark ♪</i>

466
00:26:32.667 --> 00:26:34.541
<i>♪ Just try to make it work ♪</i>

467
00:26:34.542 --> 00:26:36.500
<i>♪ To feel the fear ♪</i>

468
00:26:37.458 --> 00:26:40.707
<i>♪ Before you're here ♪</i>

469
00:26:40.708 --> 00:26:43.207
<i>♪ I make the shapes come much too close ♪</i>

470
00:26:43.208 --> 00:26:46.416
<i>♪ I pull my eyes out
Hold my breath and wait... ♪</i>

471
00:26:46.417 --> 00:26:50.833
It comes all the way
from this part here. and then it goes...

472
00:26:51.542 --> 00:26:54.832
Three. four. five.

473
00:26:54.833 --> 00:26:56.875
<i>♪ Safe and clean... ♪</i>

474
00:27:01.250 --> 00:27:04.291
<i>♪ Oh. if only I was sure ♪</i>

475
00:27:04.292 --> 00:27:07.624
<i>♪ That my head on the door was
A dre-ee-eam... ♪</i>

476
00:27:07.625 --> 00:27:10.499
-Uno. I win!
-Two of the exact same card?

477
00:27:10.500 --> 00:27:12.042
<i>♪ Mm-hmm ♪</i>

478
00:27:13.750 --> 00:27:15.250
<i>♪ Doo-doo-doo ♪</i>

479
00:27:16.292 --> 00:27:17.917
<i>♪ Doo-doo-doo... ♪</i>

480
00:27:21.167 --> 00:27:22.458
[Ann] Final demand?

481
00:27:24.292 --> 00:27:26.625
[inaudible]

482
00:27:29.250 --> 00:27:30.417
[laughter]

483
00:27:35.583 --> 00:27:39.082
-Okay. ready? One. two. three.
-[cheering]

484
00:27:39.083 --> 00:27:40.792
The perfect tree!

485
00:27:42.042 --> 00:27:44.125
Guys. look. Neighbors.

486
00:27:44.708 --> 00:27:46.375
Oh. it's so pretty.

487
00:27:47.333 --> 00:27:48.625
Christmas.

488
00:27:51.333 --> 00:27:52.416
[song ends]

489
00:27:52.417 --> 00:27:54.417
[thunder rumbling]

490
00:27:56.250 --> 00:27:58.332
[eerie creaking]

491
00:27:58.333 --> 00:27:59.999
[rain pattering]

492
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.750
-She's back.
-Who's back?

493
00:28:03.667 --> 00:28:05.000
The rain walker.

494
00:28:06.042 --> 00:28:07.542
You're so dumb.

495
00:28:08.167 --> 00:28:10.125
[unsettling piano music playing]

496
00:28:10.625 --> 00:28:12.666
[Ruth] She visits when it rains.

497
00:28:12.667 --> 00:28:14.167
[distant growling]

498
00:28:15.875 --> 00:28:17.500
I told you.

499
00:28:18.208 --> 00:28:19.417
Shut up.

500
00:28:21.542 --> 00:28:22.583
It's...

501
00:28:23.792 --> 00:28:25.750
it's probably just an animal.

502
00:28:36.417 --> 00:28:38.124
Not a lot of salad in this salad.

503
00:28:38.125 --> 00:28:39.791
If you don't want it. I'll eat it.

504
00:28:39.792 --> 00:28:42.707
We'll have more vegetables soon.
It just takes some time to grow.

505
00:28:42.708 --> 00:28:44.624
-Can I please have cereal this one time?
-No.

506
00:28:44.625 --> 00:28:47.166
This is what we're eating.
Don't get to be picky right now.

507
00:28:47.167 --> 00:28:48.916
-I'm not hungry.
-Me neither.

508
00:28:48.917 --> 00:28:50.333
Okay. then you don't eat.

509
00:28:55.542 --> 00:28:57.417
I saw someone outside today.

510
00:28:57.917 --> 00:28:59.916
-Graham saw her too.
-Just the rain. She's lying.

511
00:28:59.917 --> 00:29:01.166
-I'm not.
-You are.

512
00:29:01.167 --> 00:29:02.527
-I'm not!
-Just please just stop.

513
00:29:05.208 --> 00:29:08.582
I think that sometimes. if you stare
out the window for long enough.

514
00:29:08.583 --> 00:29:10.624
you see a lot of things
that aren't really there.

515
00:29:10.625 --> 00:29:13.749
I saw her. Mama. I did.
I think she's trying to communicate.

516
00:29:13.750 --> 00:29:18.167
You didn't communicate with anyone outside
because everybody else is locked inside.

517
00:29:24.333 --> 00:29:25.333
Sorry.

518
00:29:25.875 --> 00:29:30.207
Ru. sorry for raising my voice.
but now is not the time for stories. okay?

519
00:29:30.208 --> 00:29:33.624
Okay. Can we try and stay
a little bit more positive?

520
00:29:33.625 --> 00:29:35.291
-Yes.
-Yeah.

521
00:29:35.292 --> 00:29:39.792
I have a surprise.
I made us Christmas cookies.

522
00:29:41.333 --> 00:29:45.125
We ran out of sugar.
so I had to improvise.

523
00:29:45.708 --> 00:29:47.666
They probably taste really bad.

524
00:29:47.667 --> 00:29:49.958
Thank you. I'm sure they taste great.

525
00:29:53.125 --> 00:29:54.874
-Thanks.
-You're welcome.

526
00:29:54.875 --> 00:29:56.832
-Thank you.
-You want another one?

527
00:29:56.833 --> 00:29:57.874
I don't think so.

528
00:29:57.875 --> 00:30:00.541
[chuckling]

529
00:30:00.542 --> 00:30:03.957
[Jason] God!
Oh. this is one weird Christmas.

530
00:30:03.958 --> 00:30:06.750
Yeah. we're not screwing them up. are we?

531
00:30:07.417 --> 00:30:09.875
This is gonna scar them for life.

532
00:30:10.667 --> 00:30:13.499
We are doing the best we can for them.
That's what matters.

533
00:30:13.500 --> 00:30:15.791
-And that's what they'll remember.
-Yeah. you're right.

534
00:30:15.792 --> 00:30:20.083
This will be a distant memory one day.
and our kids are super resilient.

535
00:30:22.167 --> 00:30:24.541
Do you wanna get high
and watch <i>Air Force One</i>?

536
00:30:24.542 --> 00:30:27.957
[blows raspberry. exhales]
I'm sorry. what?

537
00:30:27.958 --> 00:30:30.957
I found one joint
at the bottom of our sex drawer.

538
00:30:30.958 --> 00:30:32.082
We have a sex drawer?

539
00:30:32.083 --> 00:30:34.749
What do you call the place
we hide the lube and toys we got...

540
00:30:34.750 --> 00:30:36.791
-Ah.
-one time for Valentine's Day?

541
00:30:36.792 --> 00:30:37.916
Yeah.

542
00:30:37.917 --> 00:30:39.750
-Yeah.
-I guess we have a sex drawer.

543
00:30:43.917 --> 00:30:45.958
Wave. Blow it up the chimney.

544
00:30:47.208 --> 00:30:49.208
[giggling]

545
00:30:49.792 --> 00:30:51.208
-She heard that?
-Just snuck in.

546
00:30:56.042 --> 00:30:58.749
"I'll do anything to save my family."

547
00:30:58.750 --> 00:31:01.749
"Don't ask me for something I can't give."

548
00:31:01.750 --> 00:31:04.916
Can you not quote the movie
before it starts? You know I hate that.

549
00:31:04.917 --> 00:31:06.832
-Yeah.
-[industrial music playing on TV]

550
00:31:06.833 --> 00:31:09.375
"Get off my plane!"

551
00:31:11.833 --> 00:31:13.416
Why do you know this movie?

552
00:31:13.417 --> 00:31:15.875
It's... I... It's a classic. Ann.

553
00:31:16.375 --> 00:31:19.041
Or I could put <i>Annie</i> on if you want.

554
00:31:19.042 --> 00:31:20.249
No!

555
00:31:20.250 --> 00:31:22.124
-No. Please. no.
-Well.

556
00:31:22.125 --> 00:31:25.042
I just need one night
without hearing those songs.

557
00:31:25.750 --> 00:31:27.417
<i>Air Force One</i>. it is.

558
00:31:27.917 --> 00:31:29.917
[dramatic drumbeat]

559
00:31:32.083 --> 00:31:33.582
[Jason] So many stars.

560
00:31:33.583 --> 00:31:37.791
[Ann] The skies clear up real quick
when no one's using the world.

561
00:31:37.792 --> 00:31:39.832
[Jason] Yeah. no airplanes.

562
00:31:39.833 --> 00:31:42.499
no helicopters. no pollution.

563
00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:44.500
[soft string music playing]

564
00:31:45.833 --> 00:31:49.000
We don't have to worry
about paying our mortgage this month.

565
00:31:49.667 --> 00:31:51.292
Hell yeah.

566
00:31:53.667 --> 00:31:56.917
This is as good as date nights
are gonna be for a while.

567
00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:09.416
You like this.

568
00:32:09.417 --> 00:32:11.082
Oh yeah. I love this.

569
00:32:11.083 --> 00:32:13.750
No. this.

570
00:32:14.667 --> 00:32:15.917
This.

571
00:32:18.125 --> 00:32:24.166
It's like you're. in a weird way.
happier in here with us.

572
00:32:24.167 --> 00:32:25.583
In a weird way.

573
00:32:26.833 --> 00:32:27.833
I am.

574
00:32:28.750 --> 00:32:31.041
Just... just a little bit.

575
00:32:31.042 --> 00:32:33.042
[Ann chuckles]

576
00:32:38.292 --> 00:32:39.833
No way!

577
00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:42.666
[Jason] Whoa.

578
00:32:42.667 --> 00:32:43.749
[Ann] Oh my...

579
00:32:43.750 --> 00:32:46.167
She's beautiful. [gasps]

580
00:32:47.458 --> 00:32:48.999
Big girl.

581
00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:50.458
[high-pitched barking]

582
00:32:51.208 --> 00:32:52.833
Good luck out there.

583
00:32:54.417 --> 00:32:56.042
It's her world now.

584
00:32:58.750 --> 00:33:01.792
We are no longer the ones
steering this ship.

585
00:33:05.875 --> 00:33:07.583
[animals chattering]

586
00:33:08.458 --> 00:33:10.999
[Ruth] Mom! Dad! Quick!

587
00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:12.500
Santa came!

588
00:33:14.167 --> 00:33:16.499
-[Jason] What you got there?
-[Ruth] Half an apple.

589
00:33:16.500 --> 00:33:17.708
[Jason] Half an apple?

590
00:33:18.458 --> 00:33:20.124
[Graham] I already have this one.

591
00:33:20.125 --> 00:33:22.208
We were sort of hoping that you'd forget.

592
00:33:24.750 --> 00:33:25.666
What is this?

593
00:33:25.667 --> 00:33:27.957
Maybe you could use it
for a pretend hair salon.

594
00:33:27.958 --> 00:33:29.083
-Thanks.
-Okay.

595
00:33:29.708 --> 00:33:32.000
This is for both of you. Whoa. whoa. whoa!

596
00:33:33.083 --> 00:33:34.124
[Ruth] Piano books?

597
00:33:34.125 --> 00:33:37.916
Yeah. you know.
the piano that your grandma got you

598
00:33:37.917 --> 00:33:40.499
that's just been collecting dust.

599
00:33:40.500 --> 00:33:42.832
-But I don't wanna play piano.
-Okay.

600
00:33:42.833 --> 00:33:44.166
-Graham?
-No.

601
00:33:44.167 --> 00:33:45.416
-We tried.
-Awesome.

602
00:33:45.417 --> 00:33:47.625
Yeah. Gray. find a present for Mom.

603
00:33:48.125 --> 00:33:50.541
What? What did you get me?

604
00:33:50.542 --> 00:33:52.750
You guys. thank you.

605
00:33:57.125 --> 00:33:58.416
It's your very first tomato.

606
00:33:58.417 --> 00:34:01.166
They saw it growing in the kitchen.
and they wanted to surprise you.

607
00:34:01.167 --> 00:34:03.457
-You grew it. Mama.
-[Ann] Oh my gosh.

608
00:34:03.458 --> 00:34:04.917
That's so sweet.

609
00:34:05.917 --> 00:34:08.249
Should I cut it so we can share it?

610
00:34:08.250 --> 00:34:11.542
-You can eat it all by yourself.
-Yeah. go ahead and eat your tomato.

611
00:34:12.917 --> 00:34:14.917
[wondrous music playing]

612
00:34:22.042 --> 00:34:23.374
It's really good.

613
00:34:23.375 --> 00:34:25.333
-I'm crying.
-Yeah.

614
00:34:37.833 --> 00:34:40.749
Mama! The old lady needs help!

615
00:34:40.750 --> 00:34:43.874
Mrs. Richardson. Take them to the den.

616
00:34:43.875 --> 00:34:44.957
-Dad.
-Let's go.

617
00:34:44.958 --> 00:34:45.957
What's happening? Dad?

618
00:34:45.958 --> 00:34:48.707
-[Ruth] Dad! No!
-Let's go. Come. Let's go. Go.

619
00:34:48.708 --> 00:34:50.750
[climactic string music playing]

620
00:35:03.333 --> 00:35:05.333
[music fades]

621
00:35:09.708 --> 00:35:11.375
Is she gonna be okay?

622
00:35:12.625 --> 00:35:14.875
No. honey. She was not okay.

623
00:35:16.208 --> 00:35:18.208
[Ruth sobbing]

624
00:35:19.583 --> 00:35:20.875
Is Christmas over yet?

625
00:35:23.708 --> 00:35:24.708
Yeah.

626
00:35:28.875 --> 00:35:30.875
[thunder crashing]

627
00:35:36.167 --> 00:35:37.167
[sighs]

628
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:39.042
That's the last of it.

629
00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:41.000
Sorry. Cass.

630
00:35:41.708 --> 00:35:43.708
Just hold it together for me.

631
00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:46.583
[rain pattering]

632
00:35:58.208 --> 00:36:00.124
[Ruth humming]

633
00:36:00.125 --> 00:36:04.291
<i>♪ Rain. rain. go away ♪</i>

634
00:36:04.292 --> 00:36:07.624
<i>♪ Come again another day ♪</i>

635
00:36:07.625 --> 00:36:09.749
-[Cassidy whining]
-[Ruth] Don't worry. Cass.

636
00:36:09.750 --> 00:36:12.125
[humming]

637
00:36:19.667 --> 00:36:21.667
[eerie music playing]

638
00:36:23.458 --> 00:36:24.999
[thunderclap]

639
00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:27.458
[jarring high-pitched whining]

640
00:36:30.792 --> 00:36:34.042
<i>♪ Rain. rain. go ♪</i>

641
00:36:34.917 --> 00:36:37.792
-[screaming]
-Please help me!

642
00:36:39.125 --> 00:36:41.125
[chilling music playing]

643
00:36:43.125 --> 00:36:45.082
-[screaming]
-What? What?

644
00:36:45.083 --> 00:36:48.499
There's a person outside. There she is!

645
00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:50.707
-What's wrong?
-Stay away from the window.

646
00:36:50.708 --> 00:36:51.708
[Ann] Why?

647
00:36:52.625 --> 00:36:54.083
[Cassidy barking]

648
00:36:55.167 --> 00:36:56.499
[woman yelling]

649
00:36:56.500 --> 00:36:57.500
Mom! Dad!

650
00:36:59.208 --> 00:37:01.457
-[Jason] Who is that?
-[woman] They're dead.

651
00:37:01.458 --> 00:37:03.833
-[Jason] It's the neighbor.
-[yelling]

652
00:37:05.667 --> 00:37:08.417
They're dead. Everyone is dead!

653
00:37:09.458 --> 00:37:11.333
Don't let them see you!

654
00:37:11.875 --> 00:37:14.957
It's over.
They're here. and no help is coming.

655
00:37:14.958 --> 00:37:17.499
-Susan.
-No help is coming!

656
00:37:17.500 --> 00:37:20.291
-We can't help you. I'm sorry.
-[Susan] Help me!

657
00:37:20.292 --> 00:37:22.500
You must... help!

658
00:37:26.833 --> 00:37:27.833
Hide.

659
00:37:31.708 --> 00:37:33.125
[screaming]

660
00:37:44.792 --> 00:37:47.292
-[wet growling]
-[Susan screaming]

661
00:37:48.625 --> 00:37:50.625
[deep rumbling]

662
00:37:51.333 --> 00:37:53.333
[roaring crash]

663
00:37:53.833 --> 00:37:55.833
[rumbling and roaring subside abruptly]

664
00:38:04.667 --> 00:38:07.375
Okay. family meeting. Right now.

665
00:38:10.250 --> 00:38:12.583
[Cassidy whining]

666
00:38:13.667 --> 00:38:16.832
-I don't know what I'm looking at.
-I've tried to tell you.

667
00:38:16.833 --> 00:38:18.957
But the one I saw seemed nice.

668
00:38:18.958 --> 00:38:21.249
Just... not like the ones tonight.

669
00:38:21.250 --> 00:38:22.958
Whatever we saw out there.

670
00:38:24.417 --> 00:38:28.083
whatever is keeping us in here.
it's... it's not nice.

671
00:38:34.083 --> 00:38:35.249
Listen to me.

672
00:38:35.250 --> 00:38:38.249
I'm not gonna let anything bad
happen to us.

673
00:38:38.250 --> 00:38:40.000
[ominous orchestral music playing]

674
00:38:41.125 --> 00:38:42.708
Can we sleep in your room tonight?

675
00:38:44.083 --> 00:38:45.083
Yeah.

676
00:38:52.583 --> 00:38:55.499
Let's limit
all signs of life visible from outside.

677
00:38:55.500 --> 00:38:58.957
-We start covering up all the windows.
-Especially when it's raining.

678
00:38:58.958 --> 00:39:00.875
Are monsters real?

679
00:39:01.875 --> 00:39:03.042
They are now.

680
00:39:03.583 --> 00:39:04.832
Not helpful. Gray.

681
00:39:04.833 --> 00:39:05.833
Sh.

682
00:39:06.458 --> 00:39:08.291
Let's settle down. okay?

683
00:39:08.292 --> 00:39:09.750
Okay. Mama.

684
00:39:11.167 --> 00:39:13.083
Sh. Go to bed.

685
00:39:22.333 --> 00:39:23.792
What do we do?

686
00:39:25.125 --> 00:39:26.417
We survive.

687
00:39:26.917 --> 00:39:28.917
[creaking]

688
00:39:38.375 --> 00:39:40.375
[creaking]

689
00:40:00.333 --> 00:40:03.499
-[Cassidy barks]
-Cassie? No. Drop it. Cassie!

690
00:40:03.500 --> 00:40:05.207
Hey! Hey.

691
00:40:05.208 --> 00:40:07.332
You know what?
You can play with Cassie later.

692
00:40:07.333 --> 00:40:09.208
Right now. let's do some PE time.

693
00:40:10.083 --> 00:40:13.999
Mom. Dad wants us to do PE. again.

694
00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:17.583
[stirring string music playing]

695
00:40:34.292 --> 00:40:35.625
[creaking]

696
00:40:43.125 --> 00:40:45.125
[clanging]

697
00:40:51.083 --> 00:40:52.083
[both] Dad!

698
00:40:54.667 --> 00:40:57.875
I think it's the chimney cap.
It must have fallen out.

699
00:40:59.875 --> 00:41:02.374
Yeah. you can see all the way through now.

700
00:41:02.375 --> 00:41:04.874
[Ann] Can you see the cracks?
Are they getting bigger?

701
00:41:04.875 --> 00:41:06.957
Cracks?
Why do we have cracks in our chimney?

702
00:41:06.958 --> 00:41:08.582
'Cause our house has structural damage.

703
00:41:08.583 --> 00:41:11.166
Does that mean the house is
gonna fall on us?

704
00:41:11.167 --> 00:41:12.416
-I hope not.
-No.

705
00:41:12.417 --> 00:41:13.707
[Ruth] Guys. who cares?

706
00:41:13.708 --> 00:41:16.207
Maybe we can get out now
through the chimney.

707
00:41:16.208 --> 00:41:20.041
It's way too narrow at the top. My weight
would make the whole thing collapse. baby.

708
00:41:20.042 --> 00:41:22.375
Then how does Santa get down the chimney?

709
00:41:25.750 --> 00:41:29.624
[giggles] Guys. I'm kidding.
Let me try going up.

710
00:41:29.625 --> 00:41:32.333
I'm the lightest.
so you can hoist me with my silks.

711
00:41:33.583 --> 00:41:35.167
[mysterious music playing]

712
00:41:44.708 --> 00:41:45.792
I'll be fine.

713
00:41:46.375 --> 00:41:47.375
Step on it.

714
00:41:47.833 --> 00:41:49.124
[Ann] Nice and slow. okay?

715
00:41:49.125 --> 00:41:50.708
-[Ruth] Bye. guys!
-[Ann] No.

716
00:41:51.750 --> 00:41:52.958
Oh God.

717
00:41:53.625 --> 00:41:55.125
Okay. I don't like this.

718
00:41:59.542 --> 00:42:02.541
Wait. I can see the cracks!

719
00:42:02.542 --> 00:42:05.249
Don't touch them. Don't touch anything.

720
00:42:05.250 --> 00:42:08.082
You were right. Dad.
I could never get through here.

721
00:42:08.083 --> 00:42:10.082
[Jason] Baby.
I'm gonna bring you down. okay?

722
00:42:10.083 --> 00:42:11.999
Wait! I wanna try something.

723
00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:14.708
[Ann] Just please be careful. okay?

724
00:42:16.750 --> 00:42:19.042
Careful! Slow down.

725
00:42:23.208 --> 00:42:25.208
[hopeful string music playing]

726
00:42:27.458 --> 00:42:29.625
[Ruth] My hand's outside the house!

727
00:42:30.167 --> 00:42:32.375
My hand's outside the house!

728
00:42:33.958 --> 00:42:35.916
My hand is outside the house!

729
00:42:35.917 --> 00:42:37.666
Mom. the weather's changing.

730
00:42:37.667 --> 00:42:39.499
I can feel the air and everything.

731
00:42:39.500 --> 00:42:42.499
Okay. that's enough.
Come down. Okay. bring her down now.

732
00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:45.333
-[Jason] Careful. careful.
-[Ann] Come on. come on.

733
00:42:48.625 --> 00:42:50.750
Take it slow. There we go.

734
00:42:51.708 --> 00:42:52.708
Almost there.

735
00:42:53.958 --> 00:42:55.166
Oh my gosh.

736
00:42:55.167 --> 00:42:56.749
-Good job. Are you okay?
-Yeah.

737
00:42:56.750 --> 00:42:59.749
Oh. my brave girl. I'm so proud of you.

738
00:42:59.750 --> 00:43:02.041
[Cassidy whining]

739
00:43:02.042 --> 00:43:04.042
What's with Cassidy?

740
00:43:04.542 --> 00:43:05.542
No.

741
00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:15.041
[Cassidy whining]

742
00:43:15.042 --> 00:43:16.458
Oh no.

743
00:43:18.500 --> 00:43:19.624
[Jason] Cass.

744
00:43:19.625 --> 00:43:21.582
-[Ann] No. don't move him.
-[Jason] Sorry. Cass.

745
00:43:21.583 --> 00:43:24.333
-Oh. my Cass.
-[Jason] It's his heart.

746
00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:27.167
-[Ann] Aww.
-[Jason] The medicine ran out.

747
00:43:29.208 --> 00:43:30.874
He had a really good life. you guys.

748
00:43:30.875 --> 00:43:34.792
-Why are you saying it like that?
-Because he's really old. honey.

749
00:43:36.167 --> 00:43:39.375
And sometimes when you get really old.
you can get very sick.

750
00:43:44.875 --> 00:43:48.624
[softly] Get the kids back to the den.
Put the TV on.

751
00:43:48.625 --> 00:43:51.874
[Ann] Okay. you guys. come on.
Let's go watch <i>Annie</i> in the den.

752
00:43:51.875 --> 00:43:54.499
[Ruth] But. Mom.
I wanna stay with Cassidy.

753
00:43:54.500 --> 00:43:55.542
[Ann] I know.

754
00:43:57.250 --> 00:43:59.625
-[mournful string music playing]
-[labored breathing]

755
00:44:02.958 --> 00:44:06.416
<i>♪ So you've gotta
hang on till tomorrow... ♪</i>

756
00:44:06.417 --> 00:44:07.541
[volume increasing]

757
00:44:07.542 --> 00:44:09.542
I know it's loud.
Cover your ears. Let's sing.

758
00:44:10.167 --> 00:44:12.416
<i>♪ Tomorrow. tomorrow ♪</i>

759
00:44:12.417 --> 00:44:14.124
<i>♪ I love you ♪</i>

760
00:44:14.125 --> 00:44:16.125
[mournful string music continues]

761
00:44:20.542 --> 00:44:23.875
[Cassidy whining]

762
00:44:28.542 --> 00:44:32.832
<i>-♪ You're only a day... ♪</i>
-[gunshot]

763
00:44:32.833 --> 00:44:36.500
<i>♪ Away ♪</i>

764
00:44:51.250 --> 00:44:52.542
You did the right thing.

765
00:44:54.542 --> 00:44:55.542
Yeah.

766
00:44:57.708 --> 00:44:58.917
I have a problem now.

767
00:45:01.458 --> 00:45:03.208
He can't just stay here.

768
00:45:06.417 --> 00:45:07.791
The fireplace.

769
00:45:07.792 --> 00:45:12.291
Like. the... a cremation.
after the kids fall asleep?

770
00:45:12.292 --> 00:45:14.375
Yeah. it's an option.

771
00:45:16.125 --> 00:45:19.541
-But there is also the freezer.
-No. we're not doing that.

772
00:45:19.542 --> 00:45:25.375
If things get bad.
like. really. really bad...

773
00:45:27.833 --> 00:45:29.500
we might wish we had that option.

774
00:45:31.500 --> 00:45:33.458
I need you to handle it.

775
00:45:34.500 --> 00:45:38.167
And I don't wanna know anything about it.

776
00:45:38.833 --> 00:45:40.833
[sinister string music droning]

777
00:45:44.125 --> 00:45:45.333
[door closes]

778
00:45:45.958 --> 00:45:47.958
[Ruth sobbing]

779
00:45:50.167 --> 00:45:51.542
Okay. It's okay.

780
00:46:48.708 --> 00:46:50.708
[stirring string melody playing]

781
00:47:22.250 --> 00:47:25.125
Yeah. Yeah. come on.

782
00:47:32.083 --> 00:47:33.875
It's all right. You can take it.

783
00:47:35.375 --> 00:47:37.000
-Yeah.
-[thunderclap]

784
00:47:53.583 --> 00:47:55.583
[music fades out]

785
00:47:56.333 --> 00:47:58.333
[low rumbling]

786
00:47:59.958 --> 00:48:02.000
[Ruth] What if doofus is right?

787
00:48:02.583 --> 00:48:04.333
Maybe they are aliens.

788
00:48:05.250 --> 00:48:07.082
Aliens can't control the rain.

789
00:48:07.083 --> 00:48:08.500
You don't know that.

790
00:48:09.917 --> 00:48:11.167
[Graham sighs deeply]

791
00:48:14.083 --> 00:48:15.542
Whatever they are...

792
00:48:17.917 --> 00:48:19.250
we're their prisoners now.

793
00:48:19.958 --> 00:48:22.625
Why would they lock us inside forever?

794
00:48:23.750 --> 00:48:24.750
Why?

795
00:48:26.042 --> 00:48:27.750
Maybe to punish us.

796
00:48:36.583 --> 00:48:39.166
[Ruth] Guess that's all the sunlight
you get today.

797
00:48:39.167 --> 00:48:41.167
[haunting piano music playing]

798
00:48:44.083 --> 00:48:46.666
-Rain. Let's go.
-I got the den.

799
00:48:46.667 --> 00:48:49.250
Let's go. You know the drill.

800
00:48:49.958 --> 00:48:51.958
[music becomes sinister]

801
00:48:54.708 --> 00:48:56.333
Let's go. Ru. Go.

802
00:48:59.875 --> 00:49:01.500
Ruth. come on.

803
00:49:02.417 --> 00:49:03.791
-Hey. what is this?
-What?

804
00:49:03.792 --> 00:49:05.374
-What's your problem?
-Okay. enough.

805
00:49:05.375 --> 00:49:07.166
Hey. don't do that.

806
00:49:07.167 --> 00:49:08.624
-[Ann] Enough.
-Don't do that.

807
00:49:08.625 --> 00:49:09.750
Okay. Come on.

808
00:49:11.542 --> 00:49:12.541
My plant.

809
00:49:12.542 --> 00:49:14.166
-Hey. Hey.
-[Ruth] Get off.

810
00:49:14.167 --> 00:49:15.416
[Jason] What are you doing?

811
00:49:15.417 --> 00:49:17.166
[growling]

812
00:49:17.167 --> 00:49:18.500
[gasps]

813
00:49:19.125 --> 00:49:20.916
[roaring]

814
00:49:20.917 --> 00:49:21.917
Don't!

815
00:49:22.833 --> 00:49:24.791
[low growl]

816
00:49:24.792 --> 00:49:26.582
[eerie music playing]

817
00:49:26.583 --> 00:49:28.666
[wet growling]

818
00:49:28.667 --> 00:49:30.667
[clattering]

819
00:49:37.667 --> 00:49:38.667
[whimpers]

820
00:49:39.542 --> 00:49:41.166
I just wanted to...

821
00:49:41.167 --> 00:49:44.874
It's okay. Hey. it's okay. It's gone.

822
00:49:44.875 --> 00:49:48.542
It's okay. You did good. You did good.
You all did real good.

823
00:50:02.917 --> 00:50:04.749
I'm still hungry.

824
00:50:04.750 --> 00:50:07.041
-We're rationing.
-[mumbled] I know. but I gotta eat.

825
00:50:07.042 --> 00:50:09.083
-So do I.
-Here.

826
00:50:12.042 --> 00:50:13.832
-Have the rest of mine.
-No!

827
00:50:13.833 --> 00:50:15.457
I want more than that.

828
00:50:15.458 --> 00:50:19.249
Just for tonight. please!
I'll go back to starving tomorrow.

829
00:50:19.250 --> 00:50:21.583
Stop it! Stop it right now!

830
00:50:23.375 --> 00:50:24.874
-Move!
-We're all hungry.

831
00:50:24.875 --> 00:50:26.166
-Let me see!
-I'm hungry too.

832
00:50:26.167 --> 00:50:27.749
Let me see in there. then I'll know.

833
00:50:27.750 --> 00:50:29.958
-I said no.
-Let her see.

834
00:50:31.458 --> 00:50:32.458
[scoffs]

835
00:50:41.708 --> 00:50:43.875
You wanna see it too? Fine.

836
00:50:58.292 --> 00:51:00.125
[Ann panting]

837
00:51:00.958 --> 00:51:02.541
[muffled] Mom! What's happening?

838
00:51:02.542 --> 00:51:04.708
[muffled] She's fine. She's just...

839
00:51:05.208 --> 00:51:06.958
[somber music playing]

840
00:51:07.458 --> 00:51:09.458
[muffled sobbing]

841
00:51:11.042 --> 00:51:12.792
[muffled yelling]

842
00:51:14.667 --> 00:51:15.667
[Jason] Okay.

843
00:51:19.625 --> 00:51:21.791
This is going to end one day.

844
00:51:21.792 --> 00:51:23.375
We'll survive this.

845
00:51:30.500 --> 00:51:31.832
No.

846
00:51:31.833 --> 00:51:34.957
It's not time for that anymore.

847
00:51:34.958 --> 00:51:36.666
It's time to be honest.

848
00:51:36.667 --> 00:51:38.499
-We're gonna starve.
-No. Stop.

849
00:51:38.500 --> 00:51:39.791
-Yes.
-No. don't say that.

850
00:51:39.792 --> 00:51:41.166
I refuse to watch our babies die.

851
00:51:41.167 --> 00:51:43.666
I'm not having this conversation with you.

852
00:51:43.667 --> 00:51:45.499
This is happening.

853
00:51:45.500 --> 00:51:47.416
No. we'll live.

854
00:51:47.417 --> 00:51:50.166
We'll do better than that. We'll thrive.

855
00:51:50.167 --> 00:51:51.708
I'll figure this out.

856
00:51:52.250 --> 00:51:53.250
Trust me.

857
00:51:54.333 --> 00:51:57.417
No. You won't.

858
00:51:58.708 --> 00:52:00.042
It's over.

859
00:52:05.417 --> 00:52:06.458
[Jason sniffles]

860
00:52:10.750 --> 00:52:12.458
[Graham] Mom. Dad.

861
00:52:13.042 --> 00:52:14.083
You could cook these.

862
00:52:17.583 --> 00:52:20.541
-Did I clean them wrong?
-No. you didn't do anything wrong. baby.

863
00:52:20.542 --> 00:52:21.666
Come here.

864
00:52:21.667 --> 00:52:23.208
[gentle music playing]

865
00:52:25.000 --> 00:52:26.833
Come here. You didn't do anything.

866
00:52:44.625 --> 00:52:45.708
[wolf yelps]

867
00:52:46.208 --> 00:52:48.167
[thunder crashing]

868
00:52:50.917 --> 00:52:52.917
[sinister music building]

869
00:52:59.208 --> 00:53:01.208
[music becomes stirring]

870
00:53:02.125 --> 00:53:03.333
Where are you going?

871
00:53:48.292 --> 00:53:49.292
Pull.

872
00:53:55.083 --> 00:53:56.624
[Graham] What happens next?

873
00:53:56.625 --> 00:53:58.042
Now we wait.

874
00:54:01.292 --> 00:54:03.208
Sh. Sh.

875
00:54:04.833 --> 00:54:07.167
[softly] Yes. Go on. grab it.

876
00:54:09.083 --> 00:54:10.083
Yeah.

877
00:54:10.917 --> 00:54:12.625
Go. go. Oh.

878
00:54:18.292 --> 00:54:19.458
[groans]

879
00:54:21.292 --> 00:54:24.333
It's okay. It's all right. [panting]

880
00:54:45.875 --> 00:54:47.374
Pull!

881
00:54:47.375 --> 00:54:48.833
[fox screeching]

882
00:54:56.375 --> 00:54:57.833
[fox whimpering]

883
00:55:08.167 --> 00:55:09.458
[exhales deeply]

884
00:55:13.792 --> 00:55:16.916
Oh no. No. no. no.
You should give it to the kids.

885
00:55:16.917 --> 00:55:19.374
You're cloudy headed.
You haven't eaten in days.

886
00:55:19.375 --> 00:55:22.833
Just eat and then go back to work.

887
00:55:38.250 --> 00:55:40.250
[music turns stirring]

888
00:56:12.042 --> 00:56:13.332
Foxes eat carrots?

889
00:56:13.333 --> 00:56:15.208
This isn't for the fox.

890
00:56:21.958 --> 00:56:23.833
[stirring music building]

891
00:56:25.917 --> 00:56:27.292
[squirrel screeching]

892
00:56:36.583 --> 00:56:37.667
What's wrong?

893
00:56:46.083 --> 00:56:48.000
[music peaks. fades out]

894
00:56:52.250 --> 00:56:53.625
[squirrel chirps. screeches]

895
00:57:01.292 --> 00:57:02.292
Chimney fishing.

896
00:57:02.875 --> 00:57:03.916
Chimney fishing.

897
00:57:03.917 --> 00:57:05.875
[tender piano music playing]

898
00:57:06.375 --> 00:57:08.667
-[Ann] Watch out. it's hot.
-[Jason] Okay. go ahead.

899
00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:16.000
[all laughing]

900
00:57:21.250 --> 00:57:24.583
So. here. I need all of this pulled up.

901
00:57:26.375 --> 00:57:29.124
[Jason] Once you get
beneath the underlayment and the subfloor.

902
00:57:29.125 --> 00:57:31.957
you're gonna get. like. a few inches
of soil and gonna hit the barrier.

903
00:57:31.958 --> 00:57:33.417
I'll make it work.

904
00:57:35.625 --> 00:57:37.417
[optimistic orchestral music playing]

905
00:57:39.375 --> 00:57:41.375
[woman] <i>Days blurred into weeks.</i>

906
00:57:42.250 --> 00:57:44.208
<i>weeks into months.</i>

907
00:57:45.042 --> 00:57:48.667
<i>People had no way of knowing
how long the visitors would be here.</i>

908
00:57:49.250 --> 00:57:51.958
<i>so they hid themselves to stay safe.</i>

909
00:57:54.208 --> 00:57:56.250
<i>Most people starved and died.</i>

910
00:57:57.208 --> 00:57:59.667
<i>Others lost hope and gave up.</i>

911
00:58:01.458 --> 00:58:04.833
<i>Still others found purpose and kept on.</i>

912
00:58:06.417 --> 00:58:07.917
[insects chirping. buzzing]

913
00:58:13.583 --> 00:58:16.958
<i>The lucky ones found togetherness.</i>

914
00:58:18.208 --> 00:58:19.541
I need more fertilizer.

915
00:58:19.542 --> 00:58:21.250
Damn. you know. I'm fresh out.

916
00:58:21.833 --> 00:58:23.333
We could make our own.

917
00:58:29.583 --> 00:58:31.541
What do you think?
I thought it was pretty good.

918
00:58:31.542 --> 00:58:32.791
Pretty good.

919
00:58:32.792 --> 00:58:34.541
[laughter]

920
00:58:34.542 --> 00:58:35.542
[Jason] Come on!

921
00:58:39.333 --> 00:58:40.708
I need more light.

922
00:58:47.167 --> 00:58:51.000
[woman] <i>The outside world
had become strange and dangerous.</i>

923
00:58:51.542 --> 00:58:55.917
<i>Inside. people found
what they needed to survive.</i>

924
00:58:59.500 --> 00:59:02.625
<i>Inside. they were free.</i>

925
00:59:08.333 --> 00:59:10.333
[thrilling music playing on TV]

926
00:59:12.708 --> 00:59:15.708
-How did they lose the gun?
-Yeah. I don't know. baby.

927
00:59:16.917 --> 00:59:19.167
<i>Ah! Ah!</i>

928
00:59:19.667 --> 00:59:22.375
<i>-Get off my plane!</i>
-[all] Get off my plane!

929
00:59:23.750 --> 00:59:25.167
[Jason] Yeah! Whoo!

930
00:59:25.958 --> 00:59:27.708
-Yeah!
-Whoo!

931
00:59:28.417 --> 00:59:29.708
Yeah!

932
00:59:34.042 --> 00:59:35.332
-[Ruth] What?
-[Graham] No!

933
00:59:35.333 --> 00:59:36.874
[Ruth] Aw!

934
00:59:36.875 --> 00:59:39.291
[Jason] We knew
this would happen eventually. right?

935
00:59:39.292 --> 00:59:42.292
Yeah. but there can still be music.

936
00:59:43.833 --> 00:59:45.250
[plays notes softly]

937
00:59:51.458 --> 00:59:53.458
[piano notes playing slowly]

938
01:00:00.167 --> 01:00:02.167
[wistful music playing]

939
01:01:33.917 --> 01:01:34.917
[Ruth] Morning.

940
01:02:27.708 --> 01:02:29.708
[bears grunting]

941
01:02:31.292 --> 01:02:33.207
[birds tweeting]

942
01:02:33.208 --> 01:02:34.958
[insects chirping]

943
01:02:56.417 --> 01:02:58.417
[thunder rumbles]

944
01:03:00.958 --> 01:03:02.375
[fox whines]

945
01:03:12.208 --> 01:03:13.208
[Ruth] Hello. rain.

946
01:03:15.417 --> 01:03:16.708
Right on time.

947
01:03:20.500 --> 01:03:22.500
[thunder rumbles]

948
01:03:24.083 --> 01:03:26.624
What will it be for you today. sir?

949
01:03:26.625 --> 01:03:29.457
The usual. fade? Side and back?

950
01:03:29.458 --> 01:03:31.958
Oh. I didn't realize
you were entertaining.

951
01:03:32.875 --> 01:03:34.874
Hey. Graham.

952
01:03:34.875 --> 01:03:36.500
You ready for your next haircut?

953
01:03:41.083 --> 01:03:42.583
[birds tweeting]

954
01:03:49.417 --> 01:03:51.375
Wow. what's that?

955
01:03:52.083 --> 01:03:54.583
I hooked up the trap to be automatic.

956
01:03:55.375 --> 01:03:57.582
[skunk chittering]

957
01:03:57.583 --> 01:04:00.582
-So no more fishing.
-That's not real fishing. Ann.

958
01:04:00.583 --> 01:04:03.500
Aren't we growing enough food now
to stop using the traps?

959
01:04:05.583 --> 01:04:07.707
[skunk screeching]

960
01:04:07.708 --> 01:04:09.708
[creaking]

961
01:04:12.083 --> 01:04:14.083
[ominous string music playing]

962
01:04:22.458 --> 01:04:24.250
[clattering]

963
01:04:25.583 --> 01:04:26.583
[metallic clang]

964
01:04:36.042 --> 01:04:38.042
[growling]

965
01:04:39.625 --> 01:04:41.083
[growling]

966
01:04:46.750 --> 01:04:48.375
[music stops]

967
01:05:09.417 --> 01:05:11.375
-[door closes]
-[Jason] Ann?

968
01:05:11.958 --> 01:05:12.874
Hey. Ann?

969
01:05:12.875 --> 01:05:15.749
-[Ann] The house is definitely sinking.
-[Jason] House is sinking.

970
01:05:15.750 --> 01:05:18.666
That's great. That's. uh... lovely.
I wanna show you something.

971
01:05:18.667 --> 01:05:20.750
Okay. no. look. It's getting worse.

972
01:05:21.375 --> 01:05:24.582
Okay? The soil is eroding under the house.

973
01:05:24.583 --> 01:05:27.041
Yeah. five years of daily rain
will do that. Come on.

974
01:05:27.042 --> 01:05:30.499
It's like whatever's keeping us locked in
is the thing keeping the house together.

975
01:05:30.500 --> 01:05:32.832
I say just let it all fall apart.

976
01:05:32.833 --> 01:05:35.832
Maybe one day
we'll be all... living in an invisible box.

977
01:05:35.833 --> 01:05:39.124
and that can be kinda cool.
Call the kids. I wanna show you something.

978
01:05:39.125 --> 01:05:41.333
[engine revving]

979
01:05:42.667 --> 01:05:44.291
[Ann] What?!

980
01:05:44.292 --> 01:05:46.292
[engine revving]

981
01:05:49.000 --> 01:05:50.916
[Jason] What you gotta say
about that. huh?

982
01:05:50.917 --> 01:05:52.624
-What?!
-[Jason] Come on.

983
01:05:52.625 --> 01:05:54.041
-Oh my God.
-[engine revs]

984
01:05:54.042 --> 01:05:55.166
-You hear that?
-[Ann] Yeah.

985
01:05:55.167 --> 01:05:56.249
-Yeah?
-[Ann] Yeah. I do.

986
01:05:56.250 --> 01:05:59.124
Nothing a little elbow grease
can't accomplish. am I right?

987
01:05:59.125 --> 01:06:01.124
Yeah. Yeah.

988
01:06:01.125 --> 01:06:03.374
Only got enough gas
to turn it on a few times.

989
01:06:03.375 --> 01:06:05.458
-[Ann] Mm-hmm.
-She really runs.

990
01:06:06.250 --> 01:06:07.541
Right?

991
01:06:07.542 --> 01:06:09.541
I mean. come on.

992
01:06:09.542 --> 01:06:11.582
-[Jason] Yeah.
-How many years?

993
01:06:11.583 --> 01:06:13.874
-Yeah. six.
-Seven.

994
01:06:13.875 --> 01:06:15.207
-Seven years!
-Give or take.

995
01:06:15.208 --> 01:06:17.999
Yeah. yeah. it's a lot of work.
Yeah. do you see this?

996
01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:19.416
[Ann] Oh my God.

997
01:06:19.417 --> 01:06:20.874
Yeah. a lot of work.

998
01:06:20.875 --> 01:06:23.207
-It's a waste of time.
-What?

999
01:06:23.208 --> 01:06:24.957
[uneasy string music playing]

1000
01:06:24.958 --> 01:06:26.375
What'd you... what'd you say?

1001
01:06:28.083 --> 01:06:29.167
No. it...

1002
01:06:30.583 --> 01:06:34.041
You built a car
that'll never drive anywhere. you know.

1003
01:06:34.042 --> 01:06:35.207
so what would you call it?

1004
01:06:35.208 --> 01:06:36.791
If you wanna work on something useful.

1005
01:06:36.792 --> 01:06:39.207
you can help me put
the dew collector up tomorrow.

1006
01:06:39.208 --> 01:06:41.832
Why? We already have all the food
and water that we need.

1007
01:06:41.833 --> 01:06:44.375
We can't rely on that forever. Can we?

1008
01:06:46.958 --> 01:06:48.333
You tell me. Can we rely on that?

1009
01:06:49.500 --> 01:06:51.957
Power's gone. Gas is gone.

1010
01:06:51.958 --> 01:06:53.167
Everything is gone.

1011
01:06:53.750 --> 01:06:55.125
But we are still here.

1012
01:06:56.375 --> 01:06:58.041
We are still here.

1013
01:06:58.042 --> 01:06:59.457
I'm here. You're here.

1014
01:06:59.458 --> 01:07:01.875
Your sister is here. Your mom is here.

1015
01:07:02.750 --> 01:07:05.500
We survive because I fight for us.

1016
01:07:08.208 --> 01:07:14.375
And if one day. Graham. this rain stops.
you bet I'm gonna be ready for it.

1017
01:07:17.333 --> 01:07:19.542
Are you done showing us your stupid car?

1018
01:07:22.083 --> 01:07:23.500
Yeah. Gray. I'm done.

1019
01:07:25.417 --> 01:07:28.250
[Ruth] Graham. come on. wait.
Graham. wait.

1020
01:07:30.792 --> 01:07:32.208
[Ann] <i>Graham's getting worse.</i>

1021
01:07:32.708 --> 01:07:34.250
<i>They're both getting worse.</i>

1022
01:07:35.083 --> 01:07:37.124
<i>This is not a childhood.</i>

1023
01:07:37.125 --> 01:07:38.957
You think
I don't think about these things?

1024
01:07:38.958 --> 01:07:41.208
You never talk about them.

1025
01:07:41.750 --> 01:07:43.208
I have one job here.

1026
01:07:43.708 --> 01:07:46.332
One job only.
which is to keep all of you guys alive.

1027
01:07:46.333 --> 01:07:49.167
We are all in here with you too.

1028
01:07:49.667 --> 01:07:52.417
This is not just your problem

1029
01:07:53.083 --> 01:07:54.500
for you to fix.

1030
01:07:55.500 --> 01:07:57.375
The kids miss their father.

1031
01:07:58.458 --> 01:08:00.833
And I miss my husband.

1032
01:08:07.500 --> 01:08:09.500
[rain pattering]

1033
01:08:13.417 --> 01:08:15.666
[Jason] It's time to help
with the water collection.

1034
01:08:15.667 --> 01:08:17.875
Shut the curtains. Let's go.

1035
01:08:37.250 --> 01:08:39.832
[pump squeaking]

1036
01:08:39.833 --> 01:08:43.167
Everybody's getting too lax
with the rules. especially you.

1037
01:08:43.875 --> 01:08:44.916
-What?
-[Jason] Yeah.

1038
01:08:44.917 --> 01:08:48.374
We're too exposed from your drawings
in the attic. and that has to end.

1039
01:08:48.375 --> 01:08:50.374
No. no. no.
You can't just take that from me.

1040
01:08:50.375 --> 01:08:51.541
-I can.
-Are you kidding?

1041
01:08:51.542 --> 01:08:52.624
-One mistake only...
-Mom?

1042
01:08:52.625 --> 01:08:53.957
And we risk losing everything.

1043
01:08:53.958 --> 01:08:55.374
How long can we keep hiding?

1044
01:08:55.375 --> 01:08:56.500
-Just...
-What's the point?

1045
01:08:57.083 --> 01:08:58.583
[growling]

1046
01:09:03.708 --> 01:09:05.708
[gurgling]

1047
01:09:07.750 --> 01:09:09.958
[softly] Hide. hide. hide. hide!

1048
01:09:11.208 --> 01:09:12.500
[Ann] Okay.

1049
01:09:13.333 --> 01:09:15.333
[tense string music playing]

1050
01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:22.000
[softly] Go. go. go.

1051
01:09:23.250 --> 01:09:25.250
[wind howls]

1052
01:09:26.042 --> 01:09:27.625
[creaking]

1053
01:09:32.042 --> 01:09:34.042
[creaking]

1054
01:09:35.833 --> 01:09:38.750
[creature growling. clicking wetly]

1055
01:09:42.458 --> 01:09:43.750
[softly] Sh.

1056
01:09:50.958 --> 01:09:52.958
[creature squelching]

1057
01:09:55.042 --> 01:09:57.042
[squelching]

1058
01:10:02.833 --> 01:10:04.792
[growling]

1059
01:10:16.583 --> 01:10:18.167
[creature roars]

1060
01:10:28.417 --> 01:10:30.499
[growling]

1061
01:10:30.500 --> 01:10:32.333
[screeching]

1062
01:10:32.833 --> 01:10:34.833
[snarling]

1063
01:10:37.792 --> 01:10:39.332
[Ann. softly] Jason.

1064
01:10:39.333 --> 01:10:40.833
The gun. Gun.

1065
01:10:42.208 --> 01:10:43.916
[creature grunting]

1066
01:10:43.917 --> 01:10:44.917
I'll go.

1067
01:10:45.375 --> 01:10:46.417
No. Stay there.

1068
01:10:51.542 --> 01:10:52.542
Stay there.

1069
01:10:57.875 --> 01:10:59.875
[growling]

1070
01:11:02.125 --> 01:11:04.125
[creaking]

1071
01:11:05.875 --> 01:11:07.250
[wind howling]

1072
01:11:25.625 --> 01:11:26.750
Ah!

1073
01:11:35.333 --> 01:11:37.458
[tense music building]

1074
01:11:40.583 --> 01:11:42.708
[Ann] Graham! Graham! No!

1075
01:11:43.833 --> 01:11:46.207
[Graham] What are you doing?
Dad. what are you doing?

1076
01:11:46.208 --> 01:11:48.207
Stop! Stop! Stop!

1077
01:11:48.208 --> 01:11:50.624
I almost got out. I almost made it out.

1078
01:11:50.625 --> 01:11:52.375
-I almost made it.
-Okay.

1079
01:11:52.958 --> 01:11:55.042
-I could've...
-[Ann] You okay?

1080
01:11:59.042 --> 01:12:00.207
That's salt water.

1081
01:12:00.208 --> 01:12:02.166
What? Hey.

1082
01:12:02.167 --> 01:12:05.332
-You okay? No. wait.
-It's seawater.

1083
01:12:05.333 --> 01:12:06.582
What?

1084
01:12:06.583 --> 01:12:09.083
Come here. away from the window.

1085
01:12:09.583 --> 01:12:11.167
Hey. hey. you guys hear that?

1086
01:12:13.833 --> 01:12:15.124
The rain stopped.

1087
01:12:15.125 --> 01:12:17.125
[solemn chords droning]

1088
01:12:18.750 --> 01:12:20.750
[birds tweeting]

1089
01:12:42.125 --> 01:12:44.125
[doleful piano melody playing]

1090
01:12:58.625 --> 01:13:00.083
[Ruth] Leviathan.

1091
01:13:01.000 --> 01:13:02.000
Kraken.

1092
01:13:03.708 --> 01:13:05.708
[creature growling]

1093
01:13:07.167 --> 01:13:08.374
[Ruth] Mermaids.

1094
01:13:08.375 --> 01:13:10.208
[distant screeching]

1095
01:13:10.792 --> 01:13:12.416
Think about it. Dad.

1096
01:13:12.417 --> 01:13:15.750
80% of the ocean floor is unexplored.

1097
01:13:16.333 --> 01:13:19.582
What if these things aren't
from outer space?

1098
01:13:19.583 --> 01:13:23.207
What if these tales of sea creatures
are real?

1099
01:13:23.208 --> 01:13:25.749
What if that's why
they can control the rain?

1100
01:13:25.750 --> 01:13:28.957
They're not conquering our world.
<i>This</i> is their world.

1101
01:13:28.958 --> 01:13:30.166
It's their home.

1102
01:13:30.167 --> 01:13:33.833
No. this is <i>our</i> home.
and you're safe here.

1103
01:13:34.750 --> 01:13:35.958
I promise.

1104
01:13:38.792 --> 01:13:39.958
If you say so.

1105
01:13:41.167 --> 01:13:42.167
What...

1106
01:13:42.625 --> 01:13:45.457
Why don't you... take a break from this?

1107
01:13:45.458 --> 01:13:46.542
This...

1108
01:13:47.125 --> 01:13:48.667
Go do something useful.

1109
01:13:52.958 --> 01:13:53.958
Okay.

1110
01:13:58.542 --> 01:13:59.583
[Ruth chuckles softly]

1111
01:14:11.792 --> 01:14:13.125
[Ann] Look at this.

1112
01:14:14.250 --> 01:14:15.625
Everything's dying.

1113
01:14:21.083 --> 01:14:23.582
Salt water. Ruthie was right.

1114
01:14:23.583 --> 01:14:26.082
That thing came in here
and poisoned all the soil.

1115
01:14:26.083 --> 01:14:29.166
It's the same with the drinking water.
We can't use any of it.

1116
01:14:29.167 --> 01:14:32.457
So that's it. then.
They starve us out like everyone else.

1117
01:14:32.458 --> 01:14:33.541
[Jason] Ann.

1118
01:14:33.542 --> 01:14:35.208
[ferret chittering]

1119
01:14:36.792 --> 01:14:38.249
[screeching]

1120
01:14:38.250 --> 01:14:40.749
-[Ann] They don't want us here. Jason.
-[Jason] That's great.

1121
01:14:40.750 --> 01:14:42.250
But where are we supposed to go?

1122
01:14:48.583 --> 01:14:51.542
We have all new tarps for collecting dew.
so we'll do that.

1123
01:14:52.167 --> 01:14:54.582
-We'll replant. We'll start over.
-You just said it yourself.

1124
01:14:54.583 --> 01:14:56.624
-We don't have water.
-It's not raining now.

1125
01:14:56.625 --> 01:14:58.624
-But it'll rain again.
-You have no idea.

1126
01:14:58.625 --> 01:15:01.999
-[Ruth] This wasn't meant for you. Hey.
-[Ann] We cannot replant.

1127
01:15:02.000 --> 01:15:03.874
You're too small to be in that.

1128
01:15:03.875 --> 01:15:06.999
[Ann] What is it you keep telling us?
Three minutes without air.

1129
01:15:07.000 --> 01:15:08.749
Three days without water.

1130
01:15:08.750 --> 01:15:10.291
Three weeks without food.

1131
01:15:10.292 --> 01:15:13.166
We have three days
before we die with no water.

1132
01:15:13.167 --> 01:15:16.791
It's not gonna come to that.
We'll have enough water to survive.

1133
01:15:16.792 --> 01:15:18.916
Just a little less than we used to.
I'll work it out.

1134
01:15:18.917 --> 01:15:21.874
What happens when that thing
comes back here? What then?

1135
01:15:21.875 --> 01:15:25.916
I don't know. Ann! I don't know!
What should I do? Shoot it?

1136
01:15:25.917 --> 01:15:28.874
Open your eyes. You think
we're still alive because of you?

1137
01:15:28.875 --> 01:15:30.999
We're still alive
because of a crack in the chimney.

1138
01:15:31.000 --> 01:15:33.916
We're not better than anyone else
who died. We're just luckier!

1139
01:15:33.917 --> 01:15:38.041
If we don't find a way out of this house.
we will die. and you know that!

1140
01:15:38.042 --> 01:15:40.041
[tense music droning]

1141
01:15:40.042 --> 01:15:41.625
-[squeaks]
-[screams]

1142
01:15:44.500 --> 01:15:47.374
-[Ruth] Oh my God. I was trying to help.
-[Jason] What is this?

1143
01:15:47.375 --> 01:15:49.582
I don't know what happened.
I... I'm so sorry.

1144
01:15:49.583 --> 01:15:51.417
I was trying to help. I didn't mean to...

1145
01:15:52.875 --> 01:15:54.916
-Is it bad?
-[Graham] Ruth. are you okay?

1146
01:15:54.917 --> 01:15:56.082
-Are you okay?
-[screeching]

1147
01:15:56.083 --> 01:15:58.416
-[Ann] Ruth.
-No! Don't kill it.

1148
01:15:58.417 --> 01:16:00.916
-[Graham] What is going on?
-Wait. Let's get this cleaned up.

1149
01:16:00.917 --> 01:16:03.541
-[Graham] Hey. what's going on?
-[Ruth] I don't know. I'm sorry.

1150
01:16:03.542 --> 01:16:05.667
-[Graham] Dad. is she gonna be okay?
-[Jason] Yeah.

1151
01:16:06.958 --> 01:16:08.832
[music turns somber]

1152
01:16:08.833 --> 01:16:10.458
[Ann] She's burning up.

1153
01:16:11.375 --> 01:16:13.417
The infection is spreading.

1154
01:16:14.083 --> 01:16:15.625
Her fever won't break.

1155
01:16:16.167 --> 01:16:17.583
We have to do something.

1156
01:16:20.667 --> 01:16:23.583
This is the last of our water.
She needs it.

1157
01:16:27.333 --> 01:16:29.000
-[coughs]
-Hey.

1158
01:16:29.917 --> 01:16:30.874
Easy.

1159
01:16:30.875 --> 01:16:32.458
We need antibiotics.

1160
01:17:15.417 --> 01:17:17.417
[engine revs]

1161
01:17:21.333 --> 01:17:22.583
[yelling]

1162
01:17:39.125 --> 01:17:40.417
[yelling]

1163
01:17:42.375 --> 01:17:45.208
-[yelling]
-[tires screeching]

1164
01:17:48.500 --> 01:17:50.167
[yelling]

1165
01:18:02.417 --> 01:18:03.750
[glass smashing]

1166
01:18:08.208 --> 01:18:09.958
[Ann. muffled] Jason!

1167
01:18:10.458 --> 01:18:14.083
Jason! Jason!

1168
01:18:18.958 --> 01:18:20.458
[Jason panting]

1169
01:18:24.875 --> 01:18:28.583
[Ann. muffled] Jason!

1170
01:18:30.250 --> 01:18:31.917
Graham! Help!

1171
01:18:34.958 --> 01:18:36.208
Come on. Come on.

1172
01:18:38.333 --> 01:18:40.082
Cracks. The cracks.

1173
01:18:40.083 --> 01:18:41.875
[hopeful orchestral music playing]

1174
01:18:43.083 --> 01:18:44.083
What are you doing?

1175
01:18:44.667 --> 01:18:45.667
[Jason grunts]

1176
01:18:54.875 --> 01:18:56.542
[Jason] The house is sinking.

1177
01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:03.249
Look at that. Look. The crack.

1178
01:19:03.250 --> 01:19:04.250
Jason!

1179
01:19:04.708 --> 01:19:06.166
[Jason] The barrier isn't deep.

1180
01:19:06.167 --> 01:19:08.499
-See?
-Jason. talk to me.

1181
01:19:08.500 --> 01:19:09.916
-See?
-[Ann] What do you see?

1182
01:19:09.917 --> 01:19:11.832
-It shifted.
-[Ann] Jason.

1183
01:19:11.833 --> 01:19:13.291
-Let me try.
-[Ann] What?

1184
01:19:13.292 --> 01:19:15.417
I can find a way out.
I can find a way out.

1185
01:19:17.583 --> 01:19:19.124
[Ann] Stop. Hey.

1186
01:19:19.125 --> 01:19:21.082
[Jason] Yes. it's deeper. There.

1187
01:19:21.083 --> 01:19:23.374
Look at me. Look at me. Jason.

1188
01:19:23.375 --> 01:19:25.291
-No. You listen to me.
-That's enough.

1189
01:19:25.292 --> 01:19:26.582
You said the house was sinking.

1190
01:19:26.583 --> 01:19:27.832
-Stop.
-Remember?

1191
01:19:27.833 --> 01:19:31.166
-Stop for a second.
-Maybe something else is shifting.

1192
01:19:31.167 --> 01:19:33.624
-You need to take a breath.
-Like the cracks in the chimney.

1193
01:19:33.625 --> 01:19:36.332
I have to try and find it. Find it.

1194
01:19:36.333 --> 01:19:37.417
Find what?

1195
01:19:38.708 --> 01:19:40.832
-See?
-See what?

1196
01:19:40.833 --> 01:19:42.583
See? Follow the crack.

1197
01:19:43.083 --> 01:19:44.541
-The crack is our escape.
-[Ann] No!

1198
01:19:44.542 --> 01:19:48.291
We have to follow the cracks.
I just have to find where the crack goes.

1199
01:19:48.292 --> 01:19:49.957
[Ann] What are you doing? Stop.

1200
01:19:49.958 --> 01:19:52.332
-Stop it. Jason!
-[Jason] I can do it!

1201
01:19:52.333 --> 01:19:53.749
Stop! Let me try!

1202
01:19:53.750 --> 01:19:55.166
I have to!

1203
01:19:55.167 --> 01:19:56.291
[Ann] That's enough!

1204
01:19:56.292 --> 01:19:58.167
Enough!

1205
01:19:59.333 --> 01:20:01.124
-You have to...
-No!

1206
01:20:01.125 --> 01:20:03.292
-[Jason yelling]
-[Ann] Stop!

1207
01:20:04.750 --> 01:20:05.792
[Ann groans]

1208
01:20:24.250 --> 01:20:25.625
It went through.

1209
01:20:27.583 --> 01:20:29.958
Stand back! Stand back!

1210
01:20:39.875 --> 01:20:41.166
Help me.

1211
01:20:41.167 --> 01:20:42.375
Here.

1212
01:20:50.542 --> 01:20:52.542
[music fades out]

1213
01:20:55.167 --> 01:20:58.374
-Where does it go?
-[Jason] It leads to the main sewer pipe.

1214
01:20:58.375 --> 01:21:00.667
The whole neighborhood is connected.

1215
01:21:01.333 --> 01:21:03.125
The Richardsons.

1216
01:21:05.375 --> 01:21:06.916
He's the dentist.

1217
01:21:06.917 --> 01:21:08.707
-He has antibiotics.
-Yeah.

1218
01:21:08.708 --> 01:21:10.791
-I just have to get in here.
-[Ann] You won't fit.

1219
01:21:10.792 --> 01:21:13.749
-I just have to make this bigger.
-Jason. the pipe's metal.

1220
01:21:13.750 --> 01:21:17.042
-I have to try.
-We don't have time. We don't have time.

1221
01:21:17.750 --> 01:21:18.832
I can fit now.

1222
01:21:18.833 --> 01:21:21.707
No. No. no. no.

1223
01:21:21.708 --> 01:21:23.083
This one is me.

1224
01:21:25.042 --> 01:21:26.667
This one's me.

1225
01:21:30.458 --> 01:21:31.667
[bleeps]

1226
01:21:33.125 --> 01:21:35.500
-[Ann] Testing. testing.
-Loud and clear.

1227
01:21:39.083 --> 01:21:40.749
[Jason] You know what I was thinking?

1228
01:21:40.750 --> 01:21:45.875
That "never put your wife down the toilet"
should have been one of my wedding vows.

1229
01:21:46.458 --> 01:21:49.250
It's a little late for that.
Don't you think?

1230
01:21:50.542 --> 01:21:51.625
Be careful. please.

1231
01:21:52.250 --> 01:21:53.375
I will.

1232
01:21:54.792 --> 01:21:57.167
And I'm bringing back medicine
for our baby.

1233
01:22:07.917 --> 01:22:08.958
Okay.

1234
01:22:11.458 --> 01:22:13.417
-[exhales deeply]
-Go.

1235
01:22:22.083 --> 01:22:23.208
Ready.

1236
01:22:29.083 --> 01:22:31.083
[eerie music droning]

1237
01:22:39.792 --> 01:22:41.625
Ann. can you see anything?

1238
01:22:45.083 --> 01:22:46.083
<i>Nothing.</i>

1239
01:22:50.792 --> 01:22:52.250
I'm gonna keep going.

1240
01:22:56.875 --> 01:22:58.875
[panting]

1241
01:23:06.625 --> 01:23:08.458
-[rats squeaking]
-[Ann yelps]

1242
01:23:22.167 --> 01:23:23.249
Wait.

1243
01:23:23.250 --> 01:23:24.416
<i>There's a loose brick.</i>

1244
01:23:24.417 --> 01:23:26.957
Okay. Ann. you should come back.
Come back.

1245
01:23:26.958 --> 01:23:29.207
[grunting]

1246
01:23:29.208 --> 01:23:31.499
[suspenseful string music playing]

1247
01:23:31.500 --> 01:23:33.833
-[Graham] Mom?
-Ann? Ann?

1248
01:23:34.542 --> 01:23:37.291
-No. Please. no.
-Mom. can you hear me?

1249
01:23:37.292 --> 01:23:38.416
Oh no. oh no.

1250
01:23:38.417 --> 01:23:39.750
Mom! Mom. come back!

1251
01:23:42.500 --> 01:23:43.500
Ann!

1252
01:23:47.375 --> 01:23:49.958
[Ann's speech distorted through device]

1253
01:23:55.625 --> 01:23:57.624
Dad! Come here right now!

1254
01:23:57.625 --> 01:24:00.333
Hurry up! Dad. come here.

1255
01:24:01.500 --> 01:24:03.458
Look. look. Come here. Hurry up.

1256
01:24:04.125 --> 01:24:07.124
-Look. Look. She made it.
-[Ann] <i>Can you hear me? Hello?</i>

1257
01:24:07.125 --> 01:24:09.249
<i>-Hey. can you hear me?</i>
-[music fades out]

1258
01:24:09.250 --> 01:24:11.082
-Yeah.
-Mom. Mom. are you okay?

1259
01:24:11.083 --> 01:24:12.833
<i>Yeah. I'm okay.</i>

1260
01:24:21.292 --> 01:24:22.542
It's Mrs. Richardson.

1261
01:24:29.625 --> 01:24:31.083
The tide came in?

1262
01:24:31.667 --> 01:24:34.667
It's like the whole house was flooded
for years.

1263
01:24:40.500 --> 01:24:42.124
We've run out of time. babe.

1264
01:24:42.125 --> 01:24:45.417
-[Graham] <i>Mom. it's starting to rain.</i>
-[Jason] <i>Ann. it's raining.</i>

1265
01:24:57.083 --> 01:24:59.749
Ann. find it and get out now!

1266
01:24:59.750 --> 01:25:01.416
I'm not leaving without it.

1267
01:25:01.417 --> 01:25:04.333
[Jason] <i>It's too late.
Ann! The rain is here.</i>

1268
01:25:05.000 --> 01:25:06.042
[Ann] Hold on.

1269
01:25:07.208 --> 01:25:08.583
Mr. Richardson?

1270
01:25:09.083 --> 01:25:10.582
Uh! Yes!

1271
01:25:10.583 --> 01:25:12.792
-[Jason] <i>What?</i>
-Yes.

1272
01:25:13.333 --> 01:25:14.832
Okay. Okay.

1273
01:25:14.833 --> 01:25:16.417
Clindacyclin.

1274
01:25:17.125 --> 01:25:18.916
-Azithromycin.
-[Graham] <i>What is that?</i>

1275
01:25:18.917 --> 01:25:20.416
-[Jason] <i>Antibiotics.</i>
-Tetracycline.

1276
01:25:20.417 --> 01:25:22.166
-[Graham] <i>Antibiotics!</i>
-Penicillin.

1277
01:25:22.167 --> 01:25:23.542
[Jason] <i>Okay. Ann. run! Run!</i>

1278
01:25:24.125 --> 01:25:26.124
-Look!
-[Jason] <i>Get out of there! Now! Come on!</i>

1279
01:25:26.125 --> 01:25:27.874
-Go! Come on!
-Go!

1280
01:25:27.875 --> 01:25:31.582
-[Ann] Look! I got it!
-[Jason] <i>Go! Go now! Go!</i>

1281
01:25:31.583 --> 01:25:33.583
[creature growling wetly]

1282
01:25:36.875 --> 01:25:38.875
[growling continues]

1283
01:25:51.208 --> 01:25:53.083
[growling continues]

1284
01:25:53.583 --> 01:25:55.583
[chilling music playing]

1285
01:25:56.792 --> 01:25:58.166
[Ann] Ah. no.

1286
01:25:58.167 --> 01:26:00.083
[creature growling]

1287
01:26:16.375 --> 01:26:18.375
[music fades out]

1288
01:26:19.083 --> 01:26:20.416
[creature screeching]

1289
01:26:20.417 --> 01:26:22.833
-[Ann screaming]
-[chilling music resumes]

1290
01:26:25.167 --> 01:26:27.167
[panting]

1291
01:26:33.042 --> 01:26:34.625
[Ann grunting]

1292
01:26:45.917 --> 01:26:47.291
I'm down here!

1293
01:26:47.292 --> 01:26:50.416
I'm here! Come on.
Throw me the silk! Bring me up now!

1294
01:26:50.417 --> 01:26:51.792
[Jason] Here. grab it.

1295
01:26:54.875 --> 01:26:56.875
[creature growling]

1296
01:27:06.042 --> 01:27:07.750
[Ann screaming]

1297
01:27:23.292 --> 01:27:24.292
You got this.

1298
01:27:26.125 --> 01:27:27.750
[creature growling]

1299
01:27:33.500 --> 01:27:35.458
[growling]

1300
01:27:41.167 --> 01:27:42.250
[grunts]

1301
01:27:42.750 --> 01:27:45.624
Here you go. Okay.
Open your mouth. Here you go.

1302
01:27:45.625 --> 01:27:47.666
We got the meds. okay?

1303
01:27:47.667 --> 01:27:50.625
Open and take it. Okay. open the water.

1304
01:27:51.292 --> 01:27:52.750
Good. There you go.

1305
01:27:53.708 --> 01:27:55.417
These should kick in fast.

1306
01:27:56.125 --> 01:27:57.749
You're gonna be okay.

1307
01:27:57.750 --> 01:27:59.791
That's my girl. Come on.

1308
01:27:59.792 --> 01:28:00.833
Okay.

1309
01:28:01.500 --> 01:28:02.500
Okay.

1310
01:28:03.292 --> 01:28:05.292
Ann. where's the gun?

1311
01:28:06.750 --> 01:28:07.750
I lost it.

1312
01:28:32.875 --> 01:28:35.042
It is going to be coming for us now.

1313
01:28:35.917 --> 01:28:38.499
It doesn't know how many of us there are.

1314
01:28:38.500 --> 01:28:40.708
You take the kids to the attic

1315
01:28:41.333 --> 01:28:42.416
and hide.

1316
01:28:42.417 --> 01:28:43.792
I'll stay here.

1317
01:28:45.125 --> 01:28:46.250
And. Ann.

1318
01:28:47.208 --> 01:28:48.958
no matter what you hear.

1319
01:28:49.625 --> 01:28:50.708
please

1320
01:28:52.167 --> 01:28:53.957
don't come out until the rain stops.

1321
01:28:53.958 --> 01:28:56.708
-You're giving up.
-This is the opposite of giving up. I'm...

1322
01:28:57.208 --> 01:29:00.541
You are going to live. All of you.

1323
01:29:00.542 --> 01:29:02.000
And you're gonna live for me.

1324
01:29:03.083 --> 01:29:06.167
This isn't living. surviving.

1325
01:29:06.958 --> 01:29:08.583
It's just not enough anymore.

1326
01:29:09.708 --> 01:29:12.207
We know that they can open that door.

1327
01:29:12.208 --> 01:29:14.499
and if they can come in.
then we can get out.

1328
01:29:14.500 --> 01:29:15.999
We'll fight them if we have to.

1329
01:29:16.000 --> 01:29:19.166
We can't fight them.
You don't know what you're talking about.

1330
01:29:19.167 --> 01:29:22.291
If there's even the slightest chance
that we can escape.

1331
01:29:22.292 --> 01:29:23.874
I'm taking that chance.

1332
01:29:23.875 --> 01:29:24.958
He's right.

1333
01:29:25.917 --> 01:29:29.250
Our family is breaking apart
trying to survive.

1334
01:29:29.958 --> 01:29:32.167
There's no life left here for us.

1335
01:29:33.375 --> 01:29:34.708
We have to try.

1336
01:29:36.917 --> 01:29:40.417
We have to escape. no matter the cost.

1337
01:29:43.167 --> 01:29:47.375
Okay. We'll do it together.
and we use what we have.

1338
01:29:47.958 --> 01:29:49.375
What do we have?

1339
01:29:50.292 --> 01:29:51.375
Our house.

1340
01:29:52.083 --> 01:29:54.416
-[purposeful music playing]
-[Jason] <i>Open up the windows.</i>

1341
01:29:54.417 --> 01:29:55.833
<i>We're done hiding.</i>

1342
01:29:56.375 --> 01:29:57.583
<i>We're gonna let them come in.</i>

1343
01:29:59.667 --> 01:30:03.208
[Ann] <i>We will do whatever it takes
to get out of here.</i>

1344
01:30:05.125 --> 01:30:07.125
[thunder crashing]

1345
01:30:11.125 --> 01:30:13.500
Hey. Can you take this?

1346
01:30:27.583 --> 01:30:29.917
[Jason] <i>Now we are going to trap them.</i>

1347
01:30:30.417 --> 01:30:32.542
<i>Graham. you'll track the creature.</i>

1348
01:30:33.042 --> 01:30:35.083
<i>Ruth. you cast the line.</i>

1349
01:30:36.583 --> 01:30:40.458
<i>Ann. you lure it to me.
and I'll set the hook.</i>

1350
01:30:40.958 --> 01:30:44.125
<i>We'll reel it in. then make our escape.</i>

1351
01:30:47.375 --> 01:30:50.583
[Ann] <i>They trapped us in here.
thinking it would kill us.</i>

1352
01:30:54.167 --> 01:30:57.958
<i>Today is our last day in this house.</i>

1353
01:30:59.500 --> 01:31:01.166
[Jason] <i>Let's go fishing.</i>

1354
01:31:01.167 --> 01:31:02.875
[music fades out]

1355
01:31:25.500 --> 01:31:26.500
Be safe.

1356
01:31:33.083 --> 01:31:35.083
[wind howling]

1357
01:31:43.625 --> 01:31:45.583
[creature growling]

1358
01:32:34.833 --> 01:32:35.833
[Jason yells]

1359
01:32:38.542 --> 01:32:39.750
[Graham] Ah! Ah!

1360
01:32:44.833 --> 01:32:46.250
[Ruth yells]

1361
01:32:51.250 --> 01:32:52.250
[grunting]

1362
01:32:54.125 --> 01:32:56.082
-[sinister music playing]
-[Ann gasping]

1363
01:32:56.083 --> 01:32:57.458
Ah! Ah!

1364
01:32:58.333 --> 01:33:00.082
-[Ruth coughing]
-[Ann] Ruth!

1365
01:33:00.083 --> 01:33:01.417
-Are you okay?
-[Ruth] Yeah!

1366
01:33:04.458 --> 01:33:05.458
[Ruth] Graham!

1367
01:33:06.000 --> 01:33:07.958
[Graham groaning]

1368
01:33:08.458 --> 01:33:09.458
Where's Dad?

1369
01:33:11.167 --> 01:33:13.417
-[Ann] Jason!
-[Jason] I'm okay!

1370
01:33:15.000 --> 01:33:16.125
[Ann groans]

1371
01:33:18.292 --> 01:33:19.542
Ah!

1372
01:33:28.458 --> 01:33:30.458
[creature roars]

1373
01:33:32.792 --> 01:33:33.958
It's here!

1374
01:33:34.625 --> 01:33:36.042
[Graham] Where's it coming from?

1375
01:33:37.667 --> 01:33:38.833
[Ann] It's gone!

1376
01:33:40.000 --> 01:33:41.000
Come on.

1377
01:33:41.500 --> 01:33:43.124
[creature growling]

1378
01:33:43.125 --> 01:33:44.582
[Ruth] It got inside!

1379
01:33:44.583 --> 01:33:47.332
[Graham] Mom. hide! It's in the house!

1380
01:33:47.333 --> 01:33:49.625
Dad! It's coming towards you!

1381
01:33:52.417 --> 01:33:54.083
[frantic string music playing]

1382
01:34:00.375 --> 01:34:02.375
[creature growling]

1383
01:34:05.167 --> 01:34:06.167
Where are you?

1384
01:34:09.167 --> 01:34:10.499
I don't have a shot!

1385
01:34:10.500 --> 01:34:12.999
Ann! Light it up!

1386
01:34:13.000 --> 01:34:14.208
Light it up now!

1387
01:34:14.875 --> 01:34:16.875
[creature gurgling]

1388
01:34:17.500 --> 01:34:19.125
[Ann grunting]

1389
01:34:21.458 --> 01:34:23.750
[creature growling]

1390
01:34:24.625 --> 01:34:25.625
It's coming back!

1391
01:34:26.750 --> 01:34:28.042
[Ann] Come on.

1392
01:34:30.083 --> 01:34:32.208
[creature screeching]

1393
01:34:34.375 --> 01:34:36.458
Ah! Ah! Ah!

1394
01:34:38.042 --> 01:34:39.417
[Jason] Gotcha.

1395
01:34:44.458 --> 01:34:45.833
-Ah!
-[Graham] Dad!

1396
01:34:53.333 --> 01:34:54.750
-Dad!
-No!

1397
01:34:55.250 --> 01:34:56.792
[Jason yells]

1398
01:34:57.750 --> 01:34:59.999
[creature bellowing]

1399
01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:01.667
-Jason!
-[Graham] Dad!

1400
01:35:02.958 --> 01:35:04.083
[Ann] Jason!

1401
01:35:07.458 --> 01:35:08.958
Ah! Ah!

1402
01:35:09.833 --> 01:35:11.582
We gotta go! Come on!

1403
01:35:11.583 --> 01:35:13.082
Come on. Dad! Come on!

1404
01:35:13.083 --> 01:35:15.583
[Ann] Hurry up! Let's go! Let's go!

1405
01:35:16.125 --> 01:35:18.542
-[dramatic brass chord]
-[music fades out]

1406
01:35:19.333 --> 01:35:22.499
The water is rising too fast!
We have to get to the attic!

1407
01:35:22.500 --> 01:35:23.707
Where's the harpoon?

1408
01:35:23.708 --> 01:35:25.375
I missed. It's in the kitchen.

1409
01:35:27.792 --> 01:35:29.582
Forget it. Let's go!

1410
01:35:29.583 --> 01:35:31.332
[Graham] I can get it!

1411
01:35:31.333 --> 01:35:32.792
I'll meet you up there.

1412
01:35:35.667 --> 01:35:36.667
Go.

1413
01:35:45.875 --> 01:35:47.875
[water gurgling]

1414
01:36:04.583 --> 01:36:06.083
[inhales deeply]

1415
01:36:06.875 --> 01:36:08.292
[inhales deeply]

1416
01:36:09.000 --> 01:36:11.000
[suspenseful percussive music playing]

1417
01:36:15.875 --> 01:36:16.917
[grunts]

1418
01:36:19.125 --> 01:36:21.458
[creature growling]

1419
01:36:27.292 --> 01:36:29.375
[creature roaring]

1420
01:36:46.625 --> 01:36:49.791
-[creature growling]
-[suspenseful music building]

1421
01:36:49.792 --> 01:36:51.167
[gasps]

1422
01:36:53.208 --> 01:36:55.167
[screaming]

1423
01:36:58.417 --> 01:36:59.417
[Ann] Watch out!

1424
01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:01.792
[Ann] Hurry! Go!

1425
01:37:02.292 --> 01:37:03.999
-[Ann] Hurry!
-[Jason] Go!

1426
01:37:04.000 --> 01:37:05.667
[Ruth] Come on! Go!

1427
01:37:06.708 --> 01:37:08.208
-Come on!
-[Jason] Run!

1428
01:37:09.750 --> 01:37:11.167
[Ann] Come on!

1429
01:37:11.708 --> 01:37:14.124
[Graham] Ruth. try the window. Dad!

1430
01:37:14.125 --> 01:37:15.917
[Ann] Come on! Push!

1431
01:37:20.458 --> 01:37:22.583
-Come on!
-[Graham] The hook. the hook!

1432
01:37:25.042 --> 01:37:27.541
[Jason] Come on. let's go.
I'm okay. I'm okay.

1433
01:37:27.542 --> 01:37:28.832
We have nowhere to go.

1434
01:37:28.833 --> 01:37:30.457
-You get this loaded!
-[Graham] Okay.

1435
01:37:30.458 --> 01:37:31.458
Quick!

1436
01:37:35.167 --> 01:37:36.457
[Graham] There you go.

1437
01:37:36.458 --> 01:37:38.249
-Ah!
-[Jason] Ah!

1438
01:37:38.250 --> 01:37:40.250
[panting]

1439
01:37:41.125 --> 01:37:43.457
Ruth. cast the line!

1440
01:37:43.458 --> 01:37:44.708
We need to find the silk!

1441
01:37:56.250 --> 01:37:57.624
It's too dark!

1442
01:37:57.625 --> 01:37:59.124
Just stay together!

1443
01:37:59.125 --> 01:38:01.083
Breathe! Take a deep breath!

1444
01:38:10.333 --> 01:38:12.333
-[creature roaring]
-[piano keys clunk]

1445
01:38:17.125 --> 01:38:19.125
[determined orchestral music playing]

1446
01:38:24.833 --> 01:38:26.583
[creature screeching]

1447
01:38:43.792 --> 01:38:45.792
[roaring]

1448
01:39:03.458 --> 01:39:04.458
[screeches]

1449
01:39:07.042 --> 01:39:09.042
[all gasping]

1450
01:39:10.917 --> 01:39:12.416
[Graham] I can't hold on!

1451
01:39:12.417 --> 01:39:13.417
[Ann] Graham!

1452
01:39:26.417 --> 01:39:28.417
[Jason yelling]

1453
01:39:32.083 --> 01:39:33.417
Go! Hurry!

1454
01:39:34.833 --> 01:39:36.708
[creature wailing]

1455
01:39:37.833 --> 01:39:39.833
[roaring]

1456
01:39:42.208 --> 01:39:43.500
[Jason grunting]

1457
01:39:44.125 --> 01:39:46.792
Open the door. or I'm gonna gut you!

1458
01:39:48.250 --> 01:39:49.958
[creature bellowing forlornly]

1459
01:39:51.417 --> 01:39:53.499
Jason. the house is coming down!

1460
01:39:53.500 --> 01:39:54.500
Let us out!

1461
01:39:59.667 --> 01:40:01.208
[Ann strains] It's not opening.

1462
01:40:02.250 --> 01:40:04.166
Open the door!

1463
01:40:04.167 --> 01:40:05.374
Dad. stop!

1464
01:40:05.375 --> 01:40:07.875
If you kill it. we'll never get out!

1465
01:40:10.750 --> 01:40:12.957
[melancholy piano music playing]

1466
01:40:12.958 --> 01:40:16.416
I tried to tell you.
but the one I saw seemed nice.

1467
01:40:16.417 --> 01:40:19.124
-It's not nice.
-[Ruth] <i>She's trying to communicate.</i>

1468
01:40:19.125 --> 01:40:21.499
-This is their home.
-No. this is <i>our</i> home.

1469
01:40:21.500 --> 01:40:23.250
[music fades out]

1470
01:40:26.333 --> 01:40:28.999
I have one job only.
which is to keep all of you guys alive.

1471
01:40:29.000 --> 01:40:31.249
This is not just your problem.

1472
01:40:31.250 --> 01:40:33.082
We survive because I fight for us.

1473
01:40:33.083 --> 01:40:36.707
You bought a gun?
What do we do when that thing comes back?

1474
01:40:36.708 --> 01:40:38.041
I don't know! Shoot it?

1475
01:40:38.042 --> 01:40:39.500
No. no. no! Don't kill it!

1476
01:40:42.542 --> 01:40:44.542
[creature squelches]

1477
01:40:45.042 --> 01:40:47.042
[creature grunting softly]

1478
01:40:51.625 --> 01:40:53.583
[creature whimpering wetly]

1479
01:40:54.167 --> 01:40:56.000
[creature grunting]

1480
01:40:59.250 --> 01:41:01.292
[apprehensive music playing]

1481
01:41:09.417 --> 01:41:11.417
[creature growling]

1482
01:41:12.375 --> 01:41:14.375
[roaring]

1483
01:41:20.333 --> 01:41:21.875
-[metallic click]
-[creaking]

1484
01:41:26.167 --> 01:41:27.500
[gasping]

1485
01:41:29.333 --> 01:41:30.833
[creature grunts wetly]

1486
01:41:38.667 --> 01:41:39.958
[creatures growling]

1487
01:41:42.708 --> 01:41:44.166
[Ruth] Mom. Dad?!

1488
01:41:44.167 --> 01:41:45.416
[Ann] It's okay.

1489
01:41:45.417 --> 01:41:47.417
[creatures squelching]

1490
01:41:51.042 --> 01:41:53.042
[creature whining]

1491
01:41:55.708 --> 01:41:57.375
[bellows]

1492
01:42:21.583 --> 01:42:23.583
[serene string music playing]

1493
01:42:33.667 --> 01:42:35.667
[hopeful piano playing]

1494
01:42:38.292 --> 01:42:39.374
Ruth!

1495
01:42:39.375 --> 01:42:41.375
[sweet string melody playing]

1496
01:42:42.458 --> 01:42:43.749
[Ann] Ruth!

1497
01:42:43.750 --> 01:42:44.750
Stop!

1498
01:42:46.292 --> 01:42:48.041
[Ruth laughing]

1499
01:42:48.042 --> 01:42:50.125
[Ann] Ruth! Ruth. stop!

1500
01:42:57.625 --> 01:42:59.625
[gulls cawing]

1501
01:43:01.500 --> 01:43:04.791
[woman] <i>Everyone remembers where they were
the day the rain stopped.</i>

1502
01:43:04.792 --> 01:43:06.332
[distant bellowing]

1503
01:43:06.333 --> 01:43:09.582
<i>It was a Tuesday. not quite summer.</i>

1504
01:43:09.583 --> 01:43:11.667
[light. determined music playing]

1505
01:43:13.625 --> 01:43:15.957
<i>For the first time in years.</i>

1506
01:43:15.958 --> 01:43:18.458
<i>my family felt hope.</i>

1507
01:43:20.292 --> 01:43:24.500
<i>In the end. an act of mercy set us free.</i>

1508
01:43:25.208 --> 01:43:29.333
<i>We showed it to them.
and they showed it to us.</i>

1509
01:43:32.333 --> 01:43:36.832
<i>We never saw them again.
but we think they're still out there.</i>

1510
01:43:36.833 --> 01:43:39.750
<i>After all. it's their home too.</i>

1511
01:43:44.042 --> 01:43:45.042
Where to?

1512
01:43:51.000 --> 01:43:52.167
Sheet the mainsail!

1513
01:43:55.542 --> 01:44:00.125
[woman] <i>My parents. my brother. and I
set off in search of a new home.</i>

1514
01:44:05.417 --> 01:44:08.792
{\an8}<i>For many years.
we felt like we were alone.</i>

1515
01:44:11.958 --> 01:44:13.292
<i>After the rain.</i>

1516
01:44:14.333 --> 01:44:16.625
<i>we knew we didn't have to be.</i>

1517
01:44:17.250 --> 01:44:18.792
[over radio] <i>Can anybody hear me?</i>

1518
01:44:19.625 --> 01:44:22.167
<i>Are there any other survivors out there?</i>

1519
01:44:26.042 --> 01:44:27.332
